{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between tartate and succinate", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between tartate and succinate is their chemical derivation: succinate is derived from succinic acid while tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Additionally, succinate is an extended-release drug that stays in the bloodstream for 24 hours, making it a once-per-day pill. On the other hand, tartrate is an immediate-release drug that does not stay in the bloodstream for 24 hours and needs to be taken at regular intervals. Another important difference is that succinate has a greater dehydrating effect and may cause side effects like constipation and dry mouth, whereas tartrate may cause diarrhea and sleep issues like insomnia or unusual dreams.", "response": "The key difference between tartrate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartaric acid.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.3, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "ground_truth": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps based on the given passages:\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\n2. If it doesn't lock, open the door and use a chisel to tap and pry off the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Remove the top door stop as well.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location using the distinct line left behind.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. If the latch still doesn't catch, tighten the hinges first.\n6. Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb if necessary.\n7. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn't align with it.\n8. Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\nFollowing these steps should help fix the door lock issue.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 2, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) (Passage 2).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper (Passage 1 and 2).\n3. Place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet lined with butter-flavored cooking spray (Passage 1).\n4. Add onion, green pepper, and tomato slices to the baking sheet (Passage 1).\n5. Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (Passage 1 and 2).\n6. To add cheesy flavor, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven for an additional 3 minutes (Passage 3).\n\nNote that Passage 3 does not provide any specific instructions for cooking the pollock, but rather suggests adding cheese to the existing dish.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake the fillets until they are cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes. After baking, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Return the fillets to the oven to allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 minutes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 3, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "ground_truth": "To fold a quilt, follow these steps:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface such as a bed or table.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n5. Finally, fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is also on the bias.", "response": "To fold a quilt, follow these steps: Lay the quilt on a flat surface. Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias. Next\nfold the lower left corner up toward the center, also ensuring the fold is on the bias. Then, fold the top left corner down toward the center, making sure the fold is on the bias. Finally, fold the top right corner down", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 77.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 4, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "ground_truth": "You can prevent birds from building nests on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch and the top of the porch if it has open rafters. This will block the birds from reaching spaces they often choose to build their nests. If you have a light fixture, you can also install bird netting over it, but make sure the netting is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs and doesn't entangle birds. Another method is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch, as this can scare birds away. Remember to move the plastic hawk periodically to prevent the birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "response": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs. Beware that the netting is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 23}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 5, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "ground_truth": "The proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold before being burned.", "response": "The proper way to dispose of a worn American flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 6, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook brats", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief guide on how to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine beer, onions, red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper in a large pot. Bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Reduce heat to medium and cook for 10 to 12 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and place them on the preheated grill.\n7. Cook the bratwurst for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\n8. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\n\nSo, to cook brats, you first prepare the grill, then cook the bratwurst in a beer mixture before grilling them until they're done.", "response": "Preheat the outdoor grill to medium-high heat, lightly oil the grill grate, combine beer and onions in a large pot and bring to a boil, submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture along with onions, butter, and beer, simmer the mixture over medium heat for 15 to 20 minutes, cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once every few minutes, for 5 to 10 minutes, serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 7, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "ground_truth": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that it runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Repeat step 4 to make two smears.\n6. Allow the smears to air dry.\n7. Label the slides clearly.\n8. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\n\nNote: It is important to sterilize the needle used to obtain the blood sample by heating it with a flame before using it. Additionally, it is essential to wear rubber gloves when handling blood to avoid coming into contact with potentially infectious materials.", "response": "To prepare a blood slide, place a clean glass slide on a flat surface, add one small drop of blood to one end, take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action, push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood, make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place in the provided slide transport containers.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 73.05, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 8, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes:\n\n1. Turn on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes.\n2. Download the audiobook you want from iTunes.\n3. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n4. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the left task pane of the iTunes window.\n5. Select the audiobook you want to sync by clicking on its title.\n6. Click \"Sync Audiobooks\" and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer.\n7. Click \"Apply\" to start the syncing process.\n\nAlternatively, you can use Syncios Audiobook Transfer to transfer audiobooks from your iPhone to iTunes. The software allows two-way transfer of files, so you can not only backup files to your PC but also transfer audiobooks from your PC to your iPhone. Here are the steps to use Syncios Audiobook Transfer:\n\n1. Launch Syncios Audiobook Transfer on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n3. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the top menu bar.\n4. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer and click \"Export\" to save them to your computer.\n5. Alternatively, you can also click \"Import\" to add new audiobooks from your computer to your iPhone.\n6. Click \"Apply\" to start the transfer process.\n\nNote that the above steps are based on the assumption that you have already turned on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes. If you have not done so, you will need to do so before attempting to sync your audiobooks.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 9, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are located in the southeastern part of the Caribbean Sea and are exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), while the Leeward Islands are located in the northwestern part of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind (\"lee\"). The main difference between them is their exposure to the wind and the resulting climate. The Windward Islands get more rain and are wetter due to their exposure to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are drier but still get rain.", "response": "The Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, while the Leeward Islands are drier but still get rain.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 10, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the process for transferring water shares includes the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, if necessary.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how water shares are transferred is: By following the steps outlined above, which include the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate, the new owner providing proof of ownership, and paying the required fees.", "response": "To transfer water shares, the seller must return the Water Stock Certificate, sign the back of the certificate, the new owner must provide proof of ownership, and a $75.00 fee must be paid.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 11, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "ground_truth": "What are the dimensions of the shed in passage 3?\n\nThe dimensions of the shed in passage 3 are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.", "response": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel, cutting two 4x4 skids at 70 2/4 inches, setting and leveling the skids, cutting two 2x6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches, and assembling the floor and setting it on the skids as shown.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 12, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "response": "When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 13, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "ground_truth": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Switch off the device by holding down the Power button for a while.\n2. Press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds until Bootloader Mode menu appears on the screen.\n3. From the menu, choose \"Factory Data Reset\" by using Volume buttons to scroll and Power key to select.\n4. Confirm the reset by pressing \"Erase Everything\".\n5. Release all keys when the process is complete.", "response": "To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps: 1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap. 2. Tap Storage Factory data reset. 3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything. 4. After that, press and hold Volum Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds. 5. Release the keys when the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen. 6. Choose the Factory Reset by pressing the Volum Down", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 14, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to soften sugar", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to soften sugar:\n\n1. Place brown sugar in an airtight container with a damp paper towel or napkin on top. Cover tightly and let it sit for a couple of days. Remove the damp paper towel, and the sugar should be soft. (Passage 1)\n2. Preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200 degrees), place hardened granulated sugar in an ovenproof container, and tap it with a spoon after 15 minutes. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave it in for an hour or two to dry out completely. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. Keep brown sugar soft by storing it in an airtight container with minimal air space between the sugar and the lid. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible. (Passage 3)", "response": "To soften sugar, you can place it in a warm oven for about 15 minutes, then tap it with a spoon to allow it to fall apart. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 15, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "ground_truth": "To attach multiple picture frames together, you can use small hinges to connect the frames. Lay the frames beside each other to determine the desired arrangement. For two frames, use identical ones, and for three frames, either choose three identical frames or use a larger one as the middle frame. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges. Attach the hinges to securely join the frames.", "response": "Lay the frames beside each other to test the effect, mark the hinge placement, and attach hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 16, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "ground_truth": "Chard is a vegetable that has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked or sautéed. Chard is in the same subspecies as beetroot and is cultivated for leaf production. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when the stems are slightly tougher. Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a minimum amount of time.", "response": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a cultivated descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It is characterized by its large, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, and is used in various culinary applications, from fresh salads to cooked dishes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 17, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "ground_truth": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "response": "To wash wine glasses properly, use hot water and mild detergent. If this method is ineffective, use baking soda to dissolve stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 18, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here's a brief answer on how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on the given passages:\n\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain for a 1.6 gallon per flush toilet.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "response": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2\n3. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n4\n5. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n6\n7. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n8", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 19, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "ground_truth": "The FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) have several differences. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another important difference is the requirement of disability. The ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, while the FEHA only requires that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the need for it to be a substantial limit.", "response": "FEHA applies to all employers, private or public, with no specific number of employees, while ADA applies to private sector employers with 4 to 15 employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability to be present, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, but FEHA requires only a limitation, not a substantial one", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 20, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "ground_truth": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove the cover.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole of the vent.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n6. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning that area as well.\n7. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access to clean.\n8. This thorough cleaning will help your dryer run efficiently and reduce the risk of house fires.\n\nNote: The information provided in the given passages is sufficient to answer the question.", "response": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 19}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 9.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 21, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "introduction to visual merchandising and relation to the consumer", "ground_truth": "Visual merchandising is a strategy used by retailers to attract customers to their store and influence their buying behavior. It involves the presentation of the store and its merchandise in a way that aligns with the retailer's goals and marketing strategy. The visual merchandiser's role is crucial as they not only help bring customers to the store but also influence their purchasing decisions, akin to \"making the horse drink\" as per G. Surrendar's analogy. Particularly, visual merchandising related to shop windows has been found to significantly impact consumer buying behavior, with variations observed based on gender and the store attributes most valued by consumers in shopping centers.", "response": "Visual merchandising is a critical component of retail strategy, designed to attract customers by aligning with the retailer's goals. It plays a crucial role in marketing, acting as a bridge between the store's offerings and the customer. The main objective of the paper is to study the influence of visual merchandising, especially the one related to the shop windows, on consumer buying behavior, considering factors like gender and store attributes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 22, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "ground_truth": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 325-350 degrees Fahrenheit. If you don't have time to defrost the roast, put it in the oven at 250 F for about an hour. Afterwards, take it out and season it with salt, pepper, and any seasonings you prefer, such as thyme, oregano or garlic. Rub the surface with 2 tsp. of olive oil. Place the roast in a roasting pan with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards, and put it back in the oven for about 1.5 to 3 hours depending on its size, or about 20-30 minutes per pound. Make sure the roast is cooked thoroughly by using a meat thermometer; the internal temperature should reach 150 degrees Fahrenheit. Once it is cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 23, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's gravitational potential energy due to its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy stored in objects due to their deformation. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane's kinetic energy in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, a baseball's kinetic energy due to its fast velocity despite its small mass, and the kinetic energy possessed by objects in motion such as cars, balls, rivers, athletes, amusement park rides, and satellites in orbit.", "response": "Potential energy examples: car moving, ball rolling, river flowing, athlete running, riding in an amusement park, satellite in orbit. Kinetic energy examples: airplane in flight, baseball thrown by a pitcher.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.99, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 24, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "avg cost to install a second floor in a house", "ground_truth": "Hiring a remodeling contractor to build a second floor addition can cost between $100-$300 a square foot for a typical addition, but the cost can go as high as $400-$500 per square foot depending on the complexity, quality of materials and local labor rates. Building a second floor can cost at least 20 percent more than building the same square footage at ground level.", "response": "$250-$350 per square foot", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 25, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\n\nThe ice water bath helps to stop the cooking process and cool down the potatoes quickly, making the skin easier to peel off.", "response": "Boil the potatoes until they are tender, then transfer them to an ice water bath. When they are cool enough to handle, peel off the skin.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.91, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 26, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make ribs", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ribs:\n\nStep 1: Prepare the ribs\n\n* Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs (passage 3)\n* Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard mixture (passage 2)\n\nStep 2: Grill the ribs\n\n* Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium heat (passage 1)\n* Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush with some of the sauce (passage 1)\n* Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs with more sauce (passage 1)\n* Continue to cook and flip every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through (passage 1)\n\nTotal grilling time: 20 minutes\n\nNote: The passages do not mention the temperature at which to cook the ribs, but a medium heat of 350°F to 450°F is suggested.", "response": "To make ribs, you can follow the instructions for grilling, preparing for cooking, or oven-cooking ribs.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 27, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, I can confidently answer the following questions:\n\nWhat is company goodwill?\nCompany goodwill refers to the positive image and reputation of a business that is built over time through providing quality products or services, satisfying customers, and building strong relationships with them. Goodwill is a valuable asset for any business as it helps to attract new customers, retain existing ones, and attract investors.\n\nWhy is goodwill important in business?\nGoodwill is important in business because it helps to build trust and loyalty among customers, which leads to long-term relationships and repeat business. A strong reputation and goodwill can also make a business more attractive to potential investors and buyers. Additionally, goodwill can help a business to stand out from its competitors and establish a unique identity in the marketplace.", "response": "Goodwill is a business asset that includes the reputation and connection with customers. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business for several reasons. It increases the customer base and retains old clients. It attracts investors and future buyers. It is the result of providing good service or product to customers, leading to their trust and repeat business. Goodwill is a valuable asset for a business and should be maintained and built upon.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 21}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 28, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between a rock and a stone", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, a rock is defined as the hard material of the earth's crust that is normally exposed on the surface or underlying the soil. On the other hand, a stone is described as a smaller piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The passages also mention that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, while rocks cannot. Therefore, the main difference between a rock and a stone is their size, with rocks being larger and stones being smaller and easier to handle.", "response": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rocks are typically larger and more substantial compared to stones.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 29, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 2:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. Select the data that you wish to sort by (in this case, the Product column (column B)) and choose alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all the cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n\nTherefore, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use either method described above.", "response": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, select the Data tab, click on the Sort button, and choose Custom Sort from the popup menu. Then select the data you wish to sort by, in this example, the Product column (column B), and click on the OK button.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 30, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "ground_truth": "To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle. You will also need to remove a pin on the outer edge of the door. Once these are removed, you can use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "response": "Remove the two screws inside the door pull cup, the one in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off the HHR rear door. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 31, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do i breed a shugabeats in my singing monsters", "ground_truth": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you must first obtain the Shugabush Monster from another island. This will turn your Shugabush Monsters into an egg. After hatching them, buy the breeding structure. Then, use the Shugabush and the Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure to get the Shugabeats monster. The order of the monsters does not matter.", "response": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you must obtain the Shugabush Monster from the other island, hatch it, buy the breeding structure, and then breed it using the Shugabush and Furcorn", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 32, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is a upc description", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, I am unable to answer the question \"What is a UPC description?\" as none of the passages provide a clear definition or explanation of what a UPC description is.", "response": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 33, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to find someone in france", "ground_truth": "To find someone in France, you can use a website for people search in France. Sending an email or letter to the Town Hall in the person's city of birth can also be helpful, especially if you have lost relatives or friends. Try to find out the person's middle name, it could make the search easier. You can also use the French white pages, available in English at www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the 'Nom' field and first name in the 'Prenom' field, enter address information if known, and then click 'Trouver' to search. For searching in Paris and its suburbs, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. Posting a missed connection on Paris Craigslist might also be helpful.", "response": "To find someone in France, you can use a website for people search in France, send an email or letter to the town hall of the city of birth, or use the French white pages (in English) at www.pagesjaunes.fr.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 34, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how is a caldera different from a crater", "ground_truth": "A caldera is a large depression caused by volcanic activity when a chamber of magma and lava gets emptied. This cavity creates pressure and the overground rocks collapse to create a large depression. On the other hand, a volcanic crater is a bowl-like structure at the top of a volcano around the opening that is used for the eruption of magma and lava. This is a depression that is the result of sinking in of the rocks because of high pressure and it typically has the opening through which lava and ash flows upwards. Craters can also be caused by impacts from meteorites, and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.", "response": "Calderas are formed by the collapse of a magma chamber underground, while craters are formed by impacts from meteorites.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 5.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 35, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "ground_truth": "Hiking as a hobby has numerous benefits for both the body and the mind. It is an inexpensive and accessible activity that can be enjoyed by individuals of all fitness levels. Hiking allows people to explore and discover beautiful natural areas, promoting a deeper connection with the environment. It also has positive effects on mental health, reducing stress and anxiety. Additionally, hiking is a cardiovascular activity that can improve overall fitness and reduce the risk of heart disease. Exposure to sunshine during hiking can also increase vitamin D levels in the body. Overall, hiking offers a wide range of benefits for individuals seeking physical and mental well-being.", "response": "Promotes mental health, exposes you to sunshine, increasing your levels of vitamin D", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 36, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "ground_truth": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\":\n\nTo change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can visit the USPS website (moversguide.usps.com), call the USPS Call Center (1-800-ASK-USPS), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. You can also use the USPS change of address feature to notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service, with secure encryption technology to protect your data.", "response": "The U.S Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure change of address service. The service can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service, and it uses encryption technology to ensure the safety of your data. You can complete the U.S. Postal Service Official Change of Address form online, visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 37, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, you can track who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as their favorite.", "response": "You can use a website like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm to track who favorited your tweets. Additionally, you can enable email notifications by going to Twitter.com, logging in with your username and password, clicking on your Twitter name, selecting the Settings option, and then clicking on the blue Notifications link.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 38, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the main factors that contribute to oily skin are:\n\n1. Genetics: According to passage 1, oily skin is hereditary, meaning that if one's parents have oily skin, they are more likely to experience it themselves.\n2. Hormonal shifts: Passage 1 suggests that hormonal changes in the body can cause oily skin to come and go.\n3. Diet: While diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin, according to passage 1.\n4. Poor hygiene: Passage 2 mentions that poor hygiene and topical applications can contribute to oily skin.\n5. Combination skin: Passage 3 defines different skin types, including combination skin, which can be prone to oily skin in certain areas, such as the T-zone.\n\nThere is no additional information provided in the passages to suggest other factors that might contribute to oily skin. Therefore, the answer to the question is based on the information provided in the passages.", "response": "Genetic factors, hormonal shifts, and diet (aggravation of acne).", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 6.7, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 39, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do raffles work", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how raffles work:\n\n1. Reverse Raffle: In this type of raffle, the numbers on the entry tickets are drawn in reverse order, starting with the last number and ending with the first number. For example, if there are 55 entries, the last number drawn wins the grand prize, followed by the next-to-last number, and so on until the first number. Each entry ticket costs $50, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket worth $1,000 and two $500 prizes (for the early bird drawing and the first ticket pulled).\n2. 50-50 Draw: This is a raffle held during a single day at a specific event. Tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roving staff with handheld electronic devices. The gross proceeds of 50-50 tickets sold at the event go into a prize pool, and 50% of the prize pool is awarded to the winner of a random draw that takes place at the end of the event. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n3. Additional Raffles: In addition to the main raffle, there may be additional raffles for drinks and dinner. These raffles are not included in the original ticket price and require separate entry fees. One of these raffles offers the chance to win $10,000!\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "A raffle works by having participants buy tickets with unique numbers. The tickets are put into a pool, and a random drawing is held to determine the winner(s). The winner(s) receive a prize, which is usually determined by the value of the tickets sold.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 40, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for various purposes such as immobilizing an injured arm, securing a bandana over a bleeding wound, and helping to keep a severe wound closed. Additionally, safety pins can be used to remove splinters in the wilderness.", "response": "Safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing an arm, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, and keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 41, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is a transistor how does it work", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, a transistor is an electronic component made of semiconductor material with at least three terminals for connection to an external circuit. It functions as an amplifier or a switch depending on the flow of electrons through its base. When working as an amplifier, it takes in a small electric current at one end and produces a larger electric current at the other. The flow of electrons is controlled by using a small amount of electricity to turn a valve-like structure in the transistor. In its off state, the holes in the base act as a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector. Transistors can have common-emitter configuration where collector current is approximately β times the base current.", "response": "A transistor is a semiconductor device that can function as an amplifier or a switch. It does this by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity, much like turning a valve to control a supply of water. The base of the transistor pulls electrons from the emitter because it has a more positive voltage than the emitter. This movement of electrons creates a flow of electricity through the transistor, passing from the emitter to the collector through the base.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 42, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "ground_truth": "To quickly get rid of mice, you should take immediate action by sealing off entry points that mice could use to enter your home. Steel wool is a good material to use for this purpose as it will prevent mice from using the hole to get back into your house. Additionally, getting rid of rats and mice involves eliminating any sources of food and shelter for these rodents and preventing them from returning.", "response": "To quickly get rid of mice, you need to take immediate action. You can prevent mice from getting back into your house by putting steel wool inside the pipe or vent before sealing it off.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 43, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "which is better exercise cycling or aerobic", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, both exercise cycling and aerobic exercise are beneficial for overall fitness.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 44, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "ground_truth": "To force removal of a printer in devices and printers:\n1. Use Print Manager or Printers folder to remove the printer or printer port.\n2. Close Print Manager or the Printers folder.\n3. Stop and restart the Spooler Service.\n4. Go to Control Panel > Hardware and Sound > Printers.\n5. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then select Delete.\n6. If the printer is connected to the computer via USB cable, disconnect it from the printer.\n7. Turn off the printer and turn it back on again. Ensure that it is in a ready state.\n8. Remove the printer from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers.", "response": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, first access the Control Panel, then navigate to Hardware and Sound, and click on Printers. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If the printer cannot be deleted, repeat the process by right-clicking the printer and selecting \"Run as administrator\" before clicking Delete again.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.34, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 45, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to guard a tall person in basketball\":\n\nTo guard a tall person in basketball, it's important to stay as close as possible to them when they're near the three-point line. Slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against them effectively.", "response": "Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 46, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "health benefits to jalapenos", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, jalapeños have various health benefits such as pain relief, weight loss, nasal decongestion, prevention of heart disease and even cancer, being full of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants. Additionally, they have cardiovascular health benefits.", "response": "Pain relief, weight loss, natural nasal decongestant, preventing heart disease, heart attack, and cancer, and being full of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 47, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "color of urin meaning", "ground_truth": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Normal urine is typically pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome. If kidney diseases are present, the filtration and re-absorption stages of urine production may be malfunctioning, altering this pale color. Red urine is typically a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Foods and medications can also affect urine color, with beets, berries, and fava beans being among the most likely to cause changes.", "response": "The color of urine can provide important clues about one's health. A pale yellow color is considered normal and is due to the pigment urochrome. However, if the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning, due to kidney diseases, the color of urine can be altered.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 48, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Wet your hair thoroughly.\n3. Apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\n4. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n5. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n6. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n7. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles.\n8. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\n\nTherefore, the steps to properly clean your hair are:\n\n1. Choose the right products.\n2. Wet your hair.\n3. Shampoo your hair.\n4. Rinse and detangle.\n5. Condition your hair.\n6. Rinse and comb.\n7. Dry your hair with a towel.\n8. Use a hair dryer.", "response": "To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 49, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is what happens when you breathe in and out:\n\nWhen you breathe in (inhalation):\n\n* The intercostal muscles contract, causing the ribcage to expand.\n* The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest.\n* Pressure inside the chest is lowered, allowing air to be sucked into the lungs.\n\nWhen you breathe out (exhalation):\n\n* The diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity.\n* The intercostal muscles relax, reducing the space in the chest cavity.\n* Air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of the lungs and windpipe, and then out of the nose or mouth.\n\nSo, in summary, when you breathe in, the diaphragm and intercostal muscles contract to bring air into the lungs, and when you breathe out, the diaphragm and intercostal muscles relax to force air out of the lungs.", "response": "When you breathe in, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage, and the diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, and the intercostal muscles relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.12, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 50, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get free voip service and phone number", "ground_truth": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can visit YouTube channels which provide tutorials on how to access these services, such as the video available at http://www.youtube.com/user/ricsil2037. You could also use cloud VoIP services that require no equipment on your end. These services offer toll-free and US local numbers that can be forwarded to any US number or used with SIP devices for outgoing calls. Additionally, companies offer DID or incoming numbers from around the world either for a flat yearly rate or a monthly fee.", "response": "To get free VoIP service and a phone number, you can visit a respected company named Google and get a free virtual phone number (VOIP) as demonstrated in a video on their YouTube channel.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 51, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "ground_truth": "To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.", "response": "To make ice cream, you can follow the instructions in the provided passages. First, prepare the base by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Heat the mixture just until it is hot. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and chill it thoroughly, at least 2 hours. Stir in vanilla extract. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 89.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 52, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nThe colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n* White represents purity\n* Blue represents patriotism\n* Red represents the willingness to shed blood during warfare\n\nThe three white stars on the flag represent the three grand divisions of Tennessee: East, Middle, and West. The blue field with the white stars is meant to symbolize the three divisions bound together as one.", "response": "White symbolizes purity, blue represents the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red indicates the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 53, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n3. Gently slide the pod into the boiling water, making sure it stays upright and no water gets in.\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and press the bottom to release the poached egg.\n\nSo, to summarize, the steps to poach an egg using a PoachPod® are:\n\n1. Bring water to a boil.\n2. Crack egg into pod.\n3. Float pod in boiling water.\n4. Cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Remove pod from water.\n6. Release egg onto plate.", "response": "Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 71.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 54, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "ground_truth": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text-only messages of up to 160 characters, while MMS allows you to send messages with pictures, sounds, videos, and text, with a larger content size of up to 300KB.", "response": "SMS allows sending text-only messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, videos, audio, and text.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "wat is dna", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, with the base pairs forming the ladder's rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. The order of the nitrogen bases in a DNA sequence forms genes, which provide the instructions for making proteins.", "response": "DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C).", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\nPassage 1 provides tips on how to repair stuck or frozen door locks, keys that don’t work, and latches that don’t latch. However, it does not specifically address the issue of a door that won't lock.\n\nPassage 2 provides instructions on how to fix a door that won't shut or lock properly by removing the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and aligning it back on. This method might work for doors that won't lock due to a misaligned door stop.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional troubleshooting steps for when a door latch won't catch due to misalignment with the strike plate. This passage suggests enlarging the latch hole in the jamb, tightening the hinges, and moving the strike plate to align with the latch.\n\nIn summary, there is no definitive solution in the provided passages to fix a door that won't lock directly. However, these passages provide general tips and troubleshooting steps that may help identify and resolve related issues such as misaligned door stops or latches. If the problem persists after trying these methods, it may be best to consult a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "response": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps: First, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 2, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "response": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, and bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 3, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fold a quilt:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, also on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n5. Fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n\nThese steps will result in a neatly folded quilt with four even corners. Note that the size of the quilt is not specified in the passages, so these steps can be applied to quilts of any size.", "response": "Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias. Fold the lower left corner up toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias. Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias. Fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 4, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "ground_truth": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves and top of your porch with staples. Additionally, you can install bird netting over your light fixture to deter birds from accessing it. Another option is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away. It's important to note that any product used to deter birds should be nonflammable and safe to use.", "response": "Use bird netting to cover the eves and top of the porch, install bird netting over the light fixture, or use a plastic hawk to scare birds away.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 20}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.95, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 5, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to either:\n\n1. Burn it in a peaceful manner, removing the blue field first and burying the ashes, or\n2. Perform a proper ceremony by folding the flag in a triangle fold before burning it.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: \"Option 1 or Option 2.\"", "response": "Burn the flag yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded\nin the customary triangle fold.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 6, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "ground_truth": "The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is unknown. However, it is believed to be a result of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in communication between the brain and the GI tract, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors may include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (either too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include diarrhea, constipation, or alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps that worsen after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, as well as a lot of gas or bloating.", "response": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, and alternating diarrhea and constipation. Symptoms also include belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement. A lot of gas or bloating. Causes of IBS are thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to alterations in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 81.08, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 7, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between essential and nonessential amino acids", "ground_truth": "Essential amino acids are ones that the body cannot produce on its own, thus they must be obtained through diet. In adults, there are eight essential amino acids: valine, isoleucine, leucine, lysine, methionine, phenylalanine, threonine, and tryptophan. For infants, histidine is also considered essential. On the other hand, nonessential amino acids are those that the body can produce, even if they are not present in the diet. These include alanine, asparagine, aspartic acid, glutamic acid, arginine, cysteine, glutamine, glycine, ornithine, proline, serine, and tyrosine. While not essential to obtain from diet, these amino acids are still necessary as they are used by the body to build proteins needed for cell repair, growth, and maintenance.", "response": "Essential amino acids are those that the body cannot produce and must be obtained from the diet, while nonessential amino acids are those that the body can produce on its own.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 8, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to sync audiobooks from iPhone to iTunes:\n\n1. Connect your iPhone to your computer using a USB cable.\n2. Open iTunes on your computer.\n3. Click on the \"Audiobooks\" tab on the left side of the iTunes window.\n4. Check the boxes next to the audiobooks you want to sync to your iPhone.\n5. Click the \"Sync Audiobooks\" button and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer or select \"All Audiobooks\" to transfer all of them to your iPhone.\n6. Click \"Apply\" at the bottom of the screen to finish the syncing process.\n\nAlternatively, you can use Syncios Audiobook Transfer to transfer audiobooks from your computer to your iOS device. To do this, follow these steps:\n\n1. Launch Syncios Audiobook Transfer on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to your computer using a USB cable.\n3. Click on the \"Books\" tab on the top menu bar.\n4. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer from your computer to your iPhone.\n5. Click the \"Import\" button to transfer the selected audiobooks to your iPhone.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "response": "To sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:\n1. Download the audiobook you want from iTunes.\n2. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the left task pane of the iTunes window.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 9, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the main difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is their exposure to the wind and precipitation. The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeasterly trade winds and receive more rainfall, making them wetter and more humid, while the Leeward Islands are located on the leeward side of the mountains and receive less rainfall, making them drier. Therefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nThe Windward Islands are wetter and more humid due to their exposure to the northeasterly trade winds, while the Leeward Islands are drier and receive less rainfall.", "response": "The leeward islands receive less rain and are drier than the windward islands.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 10, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "teresa name meaning", "ground_truth": "The name Teresa is of Greek, American, Italian, and Spanish origin. In Greek and American, it means 'Reap; from Therasia.' In Italian, it is interpreted as 'Harvester.' In Spanish, the name is associated with two popular saints, 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.' The name is also thought to originate from the Greek “therizein” meaning “to harvest, harvester” or from the Greek “theros” meaning “summer”.", "response": "Reap; from Therasia", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 11, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "difference between vietnam and india", "ground_truth": "The passages suggest that trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, particularly in the area of education. Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, where poorer children receive the same treatment as their better-off counterparts. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved setting up schools, and training teachers. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War. Both countries have a history of colonialism, with India being a former colony of the United Kingdom and Vietnam of France. Post-colonization, India experienced division and conflict among Hindus, Muslims and Sikhs. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century.", "response": "Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same deal as those who are better-off. India's early focus was on getting children into school, involving resources, facilities, setting up schools, and training teachers.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 12, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "response": "When an asset is discarded, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year. According to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961, alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with these provisions.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.12, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 13, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is psa levels mean", "ground_truth": "PSA, or Prostate-specific antigen, is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The level of PSA in a man's blood is measured by the PSA test, which involves sending a blood sample to a laboratory for analysis. The results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate conditions such as prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition like prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Total PSA levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may indicate prostate cancer, benign prostate hyperplasia, or inflammation of the prostate.", "response": "The PSA levels indicate the amount of a protein produced by the prostate gland in a man's blood.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 14, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to change the sleep time on my computer", "ground_truth": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to change the sleep time on my computer\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click the Start menu and select Control Panel.\n2. In the Control Panel, click on Power Options.\n3. In the Power Options window, click on \"Change when the computer sleeps\" on the left side of the window.\n4. In the \"Put the computer to sleep\" section, change the duration of time to the desired amount of time you want the computer to sit idle before it goes to sleep.\n5. Alternatively, you can also toggle off the option to enter Sleep mode automatically.\n\nIf you are using Windows 10, you can also search for \"Power Options\" in the taskbar search box and select it to open the Power Options window.\n\nIf you are using Windows 8.1 / Windows RT 8.1, you can move your mouse to the lower left-hand corner of the screen, right-click the Start button, and select Shut down or sign out, and then select Shut down.", "response": "To change the sleep time on your computer, you need to access the control panel or power options. For Windows 7 and 8, click Start Menu, select Control Panel, type \"power management settings\" in the search field, click \"Change power management settings,\" and then click \"Change when the computer sleeps.\" Change the \"Put the computer to sleep\" entry with the desired amount of time. For Windows 10, in the search box on the taskbar, type \"power options.\"", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 15, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some steps for attaching multiple picture frames together:\n\nPassage 1: Table-Stand Grouping\nTo join two or three frames together, you can use identical frames or one larger frame as the middle piece. Place the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect, and then mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nPassage 2: Hanging Multiple Pictures Together\nBefore attaching the frames together, test different arrangements of the group of multiple pictures on the floor. Once you have decided on the layout, screw the frames to the backer board, repeating the process for each frame. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the frames and hang them on the wall to enjoy the finished result.\n\nPassage 3: Attaching Frames Together\nTo attach two frames together, place them back to back and mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. The placement should be the same distance from the bottom edge of each frame to ensure stability when the grouped pictures are placed on a table. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nIn conclusion, the recommended method for attaching multiple picture frames together involves using identical or matching frames, marking the hinge placement on the connecting sides, and attaching small hinges to join the frames together. It's also important to test different arrangements of the group of pictures on the floor before attaching the frames together, and to ensure that the frames are securely attached to the backer board before hanging them on the wall.", "response": "Join frames by marking the hinge placement and attaching small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.]", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 16, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, Swiss chard (also known as just plain chard) is a type of beet plant that has been selected for its leaf production rather than storage root formation. It produces large, tender deep green leaves with thick, crisp stalks. The leaves have a more assertive and sometimes bitter taste compared to spinach. Swiss chard is a perishable vegetable and should be stored in the refrigerator. It can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri.", "response": "Chard is a vegetable.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 17, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "ground_truth": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "response": "To wash wine glasses properly, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles, rinse thoroughly with hot water, and dry with a smooth lint-free cloth.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.2, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 18, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "response": "Oil stains on concrete driveways can be cleaned using various methods, including oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, carburetor cleaner, and the poultice method.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 19, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "ground_truth": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like ADA does.", "response": "The difference between the FEHA and ADA is that the FEHA applies to more employees and requires a disability to be present, whereas the ADA applies to private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 20, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "ground_truth": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "response": "Step 1: Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house. Step 2: Remove the cover, the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior. Step 3: Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole. Step 4: Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Step 4: Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer. Step 5: Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 21, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "ground_truth": "The earliest signs of pregnancy often include mood swings and unusual emotional behavior due to a flood of hormones in the body. Dizziness can also occur as pregnancy causes blood vessels to dilate and blood pressure to drop. Other early symptoms can include a missed period, bloating, spotting, and cramping. Approximately half of all pregnant women experience nausea and vomiting, and around 3 in 10 women experience nausea without vomiting, with these symptoms typically starting around six weeks after their last period.", "response": "Mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, and cramping are some of the earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 22, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "ground_truth": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325 degrees F. Place the frozen roast in a roasting pan and rub the surface with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and desired seasonings. Place the roast, uncovered, in the preheated oven. Cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound or until the internal temperature reaches 150 degrees F. Once cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "response": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 23, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "ground_truth": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is needed. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring hot water is always available. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can be used to rapidly pull hot water from a water heater, while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor. However, it should be noted that heat loss from the pipes can occur, requiring the water heater to use more fuel.", "response": "hot water circulation pump", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.99, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 24, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "avg cost to install a second floor in a house", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "$100-$300 per square foot", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 25, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "ground_truth": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, first, check common tick hiding places such as inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes. Once you locate a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the tick's head where it attaches to the skin. If you plan to use your fingers, wear gloves. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Regular use of tick control products can also prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Flea and tick shampoos can kill the ticks that are already on your pet.", "response": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.03, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 26, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "ground_truth": "While you may technically lose a small amount of weight after a bowel movement, this does not come from a loss of body fat. The decrease in body weight does not come from fat loss in stools, but rather from the elimination of undigested food and waste. Weight loss is primarily tied to your caloric intake and expenditure, not bowel movements. Unless your scale is highly accurate, you're unlikely to notice a difference in your body weight before and after a bowel movement.", "response": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 27, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive feelings and loyalty of customers towards a business, gained through providing good services or products, building trust, and creating a strong reputation. Goodwill is important because it can increase customer retention, attract new customers, and make the business more attractive to investors and potential buyers.\n\nAccording to passage 3, goodwill is an intangible asset that represents the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can make the connection between the business and its customers permanent.\n\nTherefore, goodwill is important for businesses because it can lead to increased customer loyalty, positive word-of-mouth advertising, and higher sales, ultimately contributing to the long-term success and growth of the business.", "response": "Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, which tends to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors and future buyers.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.19, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 28, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between a rock and a stone", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the main difference between a rock and a stone is their size. Rocks are typically larger and more massive than stones, which are smaller and more fragmented.\n\nPassage 1 states that rocks are often used to refer to something solid, large, and grounded, such as a mountain or palisade, while stones are often used to refer to small pieces of rock or pebbles. Passage 2 defines rocks as the hard material of the earth's crust that is exposed on the surface of the earth or underlying the soil, while stones are smaller fragments of rock that can be carried in the hand.\n\nPassage 3 further clarifies the distinction by stating that rocks are made up of smaller stones, while stones are made from rocks. Additionally, rocks are described as being difficult to carry in the hand, while stones are small enough to be carried easily.\n\nIn summary, while both rocks and stones are made of the same material, they differ in size and usage. Rocks are generally larger and more massive, while stones are smaller and more fragmented.", "response": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. 2. Rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand. On the other hand, stone is just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. 3. The stones can be pelted easily but one cannot do so with rocks.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 29, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the normal b natriuretic peptide", "ground_truth": "The normal B-type Natriuretic Peptide (BNP) refers to a low amount of the BNP hormone found in the blood, produced by the heart as a measure of how well it is working. The exact normal values are not stated but are suggested to be a guide and can vary based on factors like age and gender, with values tending to increase with age and being higher in women. High levels of BNP are indicative of heart failure, with higher levels at diagnosis suggesting a more severe condition. Conversely, low levels tend to exclude heart failure.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.08, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 30, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "ground_truth": "The passage provides step-by-step instructions for removing the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR. To perform this task, the passenger must locate and remove the two screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle. A pin on the outside edge of the door must also be removed using a door panel removal tool. Once all these steps are completed, the door panel can be carefully pulled away from the frame, taking care not to damage any wiring connections.\n\nAccordingly, the answer to the question is:\n\nRemoving the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR involves locating and removing the screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle, as well as removing the pin on the outside edge of the door using a door panel removal tool.", "response": "To remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.25, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 31, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do i breed a shugabeats in my singing monsters", "ground_truth": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you need to obtain the Shugabush Monster from the other island and breed it with the Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure.", "response": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you need to obtain the Shugabush Monster from another island, turn the Shugabush Monsters into eggs, hatch the eggs, purchase and use the Shugabush Island, and breed using the combination of Shugabush and Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 32, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do twins happen", "ground_truth": "Twins are two offspring produced by the same pregnancy. They can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning they develop from one zygote that splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning they develop from two different eggs with each being fertilized by its own sperm cell. Monoamniotic twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization. Dizygotic twin pregnancies are more likely in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, aged between 30 and 40 years, of above average height and weight, and who have had several previous pregnancies.", "response": "Twins can happen in two ways: monozygotic (identical) twins, which develop from one zygote that splits and forms two embryos, and dizygotic (fraternal) twins, which develop from two different eggs, each fertilized by its own sperm cell.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 33, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to find someone in france", "ground_truth": "To find someone in France, you can use the website www.pagesjaunes.fr, the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person in the \"Nom\" field and optionally enter their first name in the \"Prenom\" field. If you know the address, you can enter it in the \"Ou\" section. Leave it blank if you don't know the address. Click on \"Trouver\" to search for the name. The search results will display the name, address, and phone number of the matching listings.", "response": "To find someone in France, you can visit www.pagesjaunes.fr, the Pages Blanches, which is the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field. You can enter a first name in Prenom. Enter address information, if known, in the Ou section. Otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. Click Trouver to search for the name. The search results will display name, address and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 74.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 34, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how is a caldera different from a crater", "ground_truth": "A caldera is a large depression created by volcanic activity when a chamber of magma and lava empties, causing the overlying rocks to collapse. It is formed by the collapsing of the ground. On the other hand, a crater is a bowl-shaped structure at the top of a volcano around the opening used for the eruption of magma and lava. It is formed by the sinking in of rocks due to high pressure.", "response": "Calderas are formed by the collapse of a magma chamber, while craters are caused by impacts from meteorites.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.02, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 35, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "ground_truth": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here are the benefits of hiking as a hobby:\n\n1. Outdoor hiking promotes mental health (Passage 1).\n2. Hiking can help increase your levels of vitamin D through exposure to sunshine (Passage 2).\n3. Hiking has a positive impact on combating symptoms of stress and anxiety (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, the main benefits of hiking as a hobby are its positive effects on mental health, physical health, and stress reduction.", "response": "Hiking promotes mental health, increases levels of vitamin D, is a cardiovascular activity, reduces the chances of heart disease, and increases overall fitness.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.72, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 36, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "ground_truth": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked if you have used third-party apps to access Snapchat. The company does not guarantee your security when using these apps and may send you a warning message before locking your account. If you have been warned multiple times and continue using third-party apps, your account may remain locked.", "response": "your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you were using a third-party application to access Snapchat.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.48, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 37, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "ground_truth": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by going to Twitter.com and logging in with your Twitter username and password. Once logged in, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, then click on Settings and finally Blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. By setting this feature, you will receive an email notification whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "response": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by setting up notifications in your Twitter account.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 38, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "ground_truth": "The floor of a tropical rainforest biome is characterized by a fast rate of decay due to the heat and moisture. This decay provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow. Various types of fruits, nuts, herbs, and mushrooms grow on the rainforest floor. Additionally, vines and ferns grow all over the rainforest, including the floor, helping to connect the various layers of the biome.", "response": "The tropical rainforest floor is characterized by a high level of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 39, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do raffles work", "ground_truth": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA reverse raffle works by having participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, usually between 1 and 55. Each ticket costs $50, and a table consists of 20 individuals who pool their money together to form a complete ticket worth $1000. There are also two $500 prizes, one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled.\n\nThe 50-50 draw is a raffle that takes place during a single event, where tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roaming staff. 50% of the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, and the winner of the random draw at the end of the event receives 50% of the prize pool. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n\nFinally, some events may include cash tip board raffles, where participants can pay to play and have the chance to win $10,000. These raffles are not included in the ticket price.", "response": "In a reverse raffle, participants buy tickets with numbers, and the highest number wins. In a 50-50 draw, the proceeds from ticket sales go into a prize pool, and 50% of the pool is given to the winner.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 40, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for the following purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to create a makeshift arm sling (Passage 2).\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg (Passage 2).\n3. Helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances (Passage 2).\n4. Removing splinters (Passage 3).\n\nThe passages mention these specific uses for safety pins in a first aid context, but do not provide any additional information regarding their use in a survival kit.", "response": "Safety pins in a first aid box are used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling, to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances, and to remove splinters in the wilderness.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 41, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is a transistor how does it work", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how a transistor works:\n\n1. A transistor functions as both an amplifier and a switch.\n2. The transistor's design allows it to control a larger supply of electricity with a small amount of electricity, much like turning a valve to control a supply of water.\n3. The base of the transistor pulls electrons from the emitter, creating a flow of electricity through the transistor.\n4. The transistor can take in a tiny electric current at one end (the input current) and produce a much bigger electric current at the other end (the output current) when it works as an amplifier.\n5. The holes in the base of the transistor act as a barrier, preventing any significant current flow from the emitter to the collector when the transistor is in its off state.\n6. When the electrons and holes move across the two junctions between the n-type and p-type silicon, the transistor begins to work.\n7. The collector current is approximately beta (common-emitter current gain) times the base current, and it is typically greater than 100 for small-signal transistors but can be smaller in transistors designed for high-power applications.\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages.", "response": "A transistor is a miniature electronic component that can function as an amplifier or a switch. It works by using a small amount of electricity to control a gate on a much larger supply of electricity. The base pulls electrons from the emitter due to a more positive voltage than the emitter. The current passes from the emitter to the collector through the base. Transistors can work as amplifiers, taking in a tiny electric current at one end and producing a much bigger electric current at the other.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 42, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to quickly get rid of mice:\n\n1. Take immediate action to get rid of mice as soon as possible, as they can quickly take up residence in your home and start nesting (Passage 1).\n2. Seal off all entry points into your home, including holes around pipes and vents, using steel wool to prevent mice from getting back in (Passage 2).\n3. Get rid of any sources of food for mice and rats, as they will quickly take advantage of any food left behind by humans (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to quickly get rid of mice once they have entered a home.", "response": "The best way to get rid of mice is to take immediate action.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 43, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "which is better exercise cycling or aerobic", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it appears that both cycling and aerobic exercise have their benefits, but there are some differences to consider.\n\nPassage 2 suggests that cycling may be more suitable for individuals with arthritic or orthopedic problems due to its low-impact nature. Additionally, passage 3 states that stationary cycling provides the lowest impact workout compared to other indoor exercises like the treadmill and rowing machine.\n\nHowever, it's important to note that aerobic exercise, such as running, can also be beneficial for overall health and fitness. Passage 1 encourages individuals to view a wide variety of physical activities as challenges and find their fitness Zen, suggesting that different types of exercise may be better suited to different people depending on their goals and preferences.\n\nTherefore, I cannot definitively say which is better, cycling or aerobic exercise, based on the given passages. Both types of exercise have their advantages and disadvantages, and the best choice will depend on the individual's specific needs and goals.", "response": "Cycling is a type of aerobic exercise that is suitable for individuals with arthritic or orthopedic issues, providing a low-impact workout compared to other indoor exercise machines.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 44, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the information provided in the passages, here are the steps to force remove a printer in Devices and Printers:\n\n1. Open Print Manager or Printers folder.\n2. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you can't delete the printer, run the command with administrative privileges by right-clicking the printer again and selecting \"Run as administrator\" before deleting it.\n3. Alternatively, you can remove the printer from the devices list, uninstall the Windows print drivers, and disconnect the printer from the computer if it's connected via USB. Restart the Spooler Service after removing the printer or printer port.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 45, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "ground_truth": "The nervous system and endocrine system are both critical to maintaining homeostasis in the body by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. They both use chemical messengers, although their method of transmission and release differs. The nervous system is made of interconnected neuron cells and uses electrochemical pulses for signal transmission. In contrast, the endocrine system is made of discrete glands that use hormones for signal transmission and utilizes the circulatory system to carry these signals.", "response": "The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system. The nervous system is continuous and interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 46, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "health benefits to jalapenos", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are some health benefits of jalapenos:\n\n* Pain relief\n* Weight loss\n* Natural nasal decongestant\n* May help prevent heart disease, heart attack, and cancer\n* Good source of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants\n* Cardiovascular health benefits, including defending against heart health concerns and increasing cardiovascular health benefits.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What are the health benefits of jalapenos?\" can be summarized as:\n\n* Pain relief\n* Weight loss\n* Nasal decongestant\n* Anti-cancer properties\n* Cardiovascular health benefits\n* Rich in vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants.", "response": "Pain relief, weight loss, nasal decongestant, cardiovascular health benefits, and potential prevention of heart disease, heart attack, and cancer.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 47, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "color of urin meaning", "ground_truth": "The color of urine can indicate different health conditions. Red urine may indicate the presence of blood and could be a sign of an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine can be a characteristic of porphyria, a rare disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome.", "response": "The color of urine can provide insight into one's health. For instance, red or purple urine can signify blood in the urine or porphyria, respectively. Pale yellow urine, on the other hand, is the normal color and is attributed to the pigment urochrome. Changes in the color of urine can be caused by various factors, including diseases like kidney diseases, certain foods such as beets, berries, and fava beans, and medications.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 48, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "ground_truth": "Vinegar can be used to improve a dog's skin and coat, clean out their ears, repel fleas, and soothe itchy ears.", "response": "improving skin and coat health, cleaning ears, repelling fleas, fighting fleas, and soothing itchy ears.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 49, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "ground_truth": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nWhen you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, increasing the volume of the chest cavity. This lowers the pressure inside the chest, allowing air to enter the lungs. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract, expanding the ribcage and further increasing the space in the chest cavity. Air enters the lungs through the windpipe (trachea) and fills the expanded lung tissue.\n\nWhen you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax, allowing the chest cavity to decrease in size. As the space in the chest cavity decreases, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of the lungs and windpipe, and then out of the nose or mouth.\n\nTherefore, when you breathe in and out, air enters the lungs during inhalation and leaves the lungs during exhalation.", "response": "When you breathe in (inspiration), the diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. The intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribc", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 50, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get free voip service and phone number", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to get free VoIP service and phone numbers:\n\n1. Free DID (incoming numbers) from around the world: There are several companies offering free or paid VoIP services that provide incoming numbers from around the world. These numbers can be obtained by signing up for a VoIP service provider and paying a flat yearly rate or monthly fee.\n2. Get a free Virtual Phone Number (VOIP) from Google: According to the passage, Google offers free virtual phone numbers that can be used to place and receive calls using the internet. To get a free number, visit the author's YouTube channel and follow the instructions provided.\n3. Cloud VoIP Service: The passage mentions a cloud VoIP service that provides toll-free numbers and US local numbers that can be forwarded to any US number (including cell phones) or used with a SIP device. While there is no direct mention of free service, the passage does indicate that the pricing has been lowered.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. None of the passages provide detailed information on how to get free VoIP service and phone numbers without any additional costs or requirements.", "response": "To get a free VoIP service and phone number, you can consider services that offer free DID (incoming numbers) from around the world.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 51, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "ground_truth": "To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to manufacturer's instructions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. For a creamy and flavorful base, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly before using it as a base for your desired ice cream flavor.", "response": "First, mix the base, as described in passage 3. Then, churn the mix according to manufacturer's directions, as described in passage 1.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 52, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the colors of the Tennessee flag are said to have the following meanings:\n\n* White: Purity\n* Red: Readiness to shed blood during warfare\n* Blue: Patriotism of the people of Tennessee\n\nTherefore, the colors of the Tennessee flag are meant to symbolize the state's patriotism, willingness to defend itself, and purity.", "response": "White is a symbol of purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 53, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "weather in wellesley", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "The weather in Wellesley during the provided days in August varied from sunny to moderate or heavy rain. On Tuesday, Wednesday, and Sunday, the weather was mostly sunny with temperatures ranging from 79 to 83 degrees. On Monday, the weather was described as moderate or heavy rain in the area with thunder, and the temperature was 77 degrees.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 54, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "response": "SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows for sending text as well as pictures, sounds, videos, or any combination of the four.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to grill a porterhouse", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain any information or instructions on how to grill a Porterhouse steak specifically. While they do provide general guidance on setting up a grill and preparing the grill grate, they do not offer any specific advice or steps for cooking a Porterhouse steak. Therefore, I cannot provide a response based on the given passages.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check the door stop: According to passage 2, if the door won't lock, try tapping the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Then, place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\n2. Adjust the latch hole: If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, as suggested in passage 3. Before doing so, tighten the hinges first. Additionally, you may need to enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate.\n\nIf the passages do not provide sufficient information to answer the question, the response would be: \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "response": "Use a chisel to remove the door stop and adjust its position.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 2, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "ground_truth": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior. You can then apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Afterward, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. You can mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. Some plastic may be extremely difficult to remove, in which case you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun and then peel it off. If not all plastic comes off, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "response": "Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 72.94, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 3, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fold a quilt:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n5. Fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How to fold a quilt\" can be summarized in five steps:\n\n1. Lay the quilt flat.\n2. Fold lower right corner up.\n3. Fold lower left corner up.\n4. Fold top left corner down.\n5. Fold top right corner down.", "response": "To fold a quilt, lay the quilt on a flat surface. Fold the lower right corner up toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias. Fold the lower left corner up toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias. Fold the top left corner down toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias. Fold the top right corner down toward the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 4, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This will prevent birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests, which can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease. (Passage 1:4)\n2. Install bird netting over the top of your light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs, and make sure it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. (Passage 2:1)\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch. Move the plastic hawk periodically to keep the birds from becoming accustomed to its presence. (Passage 3:1)\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, you can keep birds from building nests on your porch by using bird netting, installing bird netting over your light fixture, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch.", "response": "Use bird netting around the perimeter of the porch and over light fixtures, and mount a plastic hawk on or near the porch.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 17}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 5, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to either:\n\n1. Remove the blue field and burn it in a peaceful manner, then bury the ashes.\n2. Fold the flag in the customary triangle fold and burn it in a proper ceremony.\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n1. Remove the blue field and burn it, or\n2. Fold the flag in the customary triangle fold and burn it in a proper ceremony.", "response": "The proper way to dispose of a worn American flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.19, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 6, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "ground_truth": "Symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of irritable bowel syndrome are unknown but it is believed to be due to a number of factors including alteration in gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "response": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, alternating diarrhea and constipation, belly pains or cramps, gas or bloating.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 17}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 7, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between essential and nonessential amino acids", "ground_truth": "Essential amino acids are those that cannot be made by the body and must be obtained from the diet. Adults need to obtain eight essential amino acids: valine, isoleucine, leucine, lysine, methionine, phenylalanine, threonine, and tryptophan. The ninth essential amino acid, histidine, is only essential for infants. Nonessential amino acids, on the other hand, can be made by the body from essential amino acids or by breaking down protein products. Some examples of nonessential amino acids are alanine, asparagine, aspartic acid, glutamic acid, arginine, cysteine, glutamine, glycine, ornithine, proline, serine, and tyrosine.", "response": "Essential amino acids are those that the body cannot produce and must be obtained from the diet, while nonessential amino acids can be produced by the body and do not need to be obtained from the diet.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 8, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how the body systems work together", "ground_truth": "The various systems in the human body work together to ensure its normal functioning. For instance, the urinary system works with all other systems to clean the blood by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. This includes organs like the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system also collaborates with all other systems to provide oxygen to all body parts and remove carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The respiratory system comprises the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.", "response": "The body systems work together by each system having specific roles and responsibilities, but they are interconnected and dependent on each other.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 7.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 18}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 9, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "response": "The Leeward Islands are drier and farther from the shore, while the Windward Islands are closer to the ocean and receive more rain.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 10, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "teresa name meaning", "ground_truth": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "response": "Reap; from Therasia", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 11, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "ground_truth": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but keep the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices if you like. Roasting time is dependent on the size of the cloves and may take up to 45 minutes or an hour for larger cloves. Once roasted, the garlic cloves can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 70.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 12, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nAccording to passage 1, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\n\nPassage 3 further states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the block value of the asset by the scrap value in the previous year in which it is discarded, and to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset in the year of discard and subsequent years.", "response": "The treatment when an asset is discarded under the Income Tax Act involves reducing the scrap value of the asset from the block in the previous year. All assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 13, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is psa levels mean", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels refer to the amount of prostate-specific antigen present in a man's blood. The level of PSA is measured in nanograms per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Normal PSA levels range between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml, and a moderate elevation in PSA levels may require further testing, such as a free PSA test, to determine the ratio of free to total PSA and help distinguish between prostate cancer and other non-cancer causes of elevated PSA. Therefore, the PSA test is used to monitor the progression of prostate cancer and to detect elevated PSA levels that may indicate prostate cancer or other prostate issues.", "response": "The PSA levels measure the amount of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) in a man's blood, which is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.03, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 14, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "ground_truth": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "response": "Psychological effects of hugging include reducing worry of mortality and improving self-esteem.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.08, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 15, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding (Passage 1).\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect (Passage 1).\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, making sure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame (Passage 1).\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames (Passage 1).\n5. Test ideas by laying the group of multiple pictures out on the floor first (Passage 2).\n6. Screw the frame to the backer board, repeat with each frame, and attach a hanging wire to the back (Passage 3).\n\nIt's important to note that the passages do not provide specific information on how to attach multiple frames together other than the steps mentioned above. Therefore, if more detailed instructions are needed, it may be best to consult additional resources or seek advice from a professional framer.", "response": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.94, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 16, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is what can be inferred about the vegetable \"chard\":\n\n* Chard is a type of beet (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) that has been chosen for leaf production over storage root formation.\n* Chard has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\n* The flavor of chard is similar to spinach but with a stronger, more assertive taste (some consider it bitter).\n* Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked to reduce bitterness and bring out a refined flavor.\n* Chard is an attractive ornamental plant that adds color to the vegetable garden.\n* Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator to minimize spoilage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is chard vegetable?\" is: A beet variety (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) grown for leaf production, characterized by large, fleshy leaves and stalks with a strong, bitter flavor that becomes more refined with cooking.", "response": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 17, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda and hot water to remove wine residue, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass after rinsing it thoroughly with hot water, and dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 17}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 18, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "average weather sausalito", "ground_truth": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "response": "The average weather in Sausalito includes a high of around 69 degrees in July and a low of 43 degrees in January. It receives 34 inches of rain per year with no snowfall.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 19, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) are:\n\n1. Scope of application: The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\n2. Definition of disability: The FEHA requires that a disability must limit a major life activity, while the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity.\n3. Number of employees: The ADA applies to employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA has no such requirement.\n\nTherefore, the main difference between FEHA and ADA is the scope of application and the definition of disability.", "response": "FEHA applies to more employees than ADA, doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like ADA does, requires a disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, and is specifically designed for supervisors and managers to understand their responsibilities during the reasonable accommodation process.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 17}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 20, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the steps to clean a dryer vent based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house (passage 1) and remove it by sliding it out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the exterior (step 2).\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the hole where the vent connects to the dryer (step 3).\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint (step 4).\n4. Clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (step 4).\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (step 5).\n6. If desired, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter (passage 2).\n7. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits in the area around the lint filter frame (passage 2).\n\nNote: Passage 3 provides additional information but does not provide specific instructions for cleaning the dryer vent. Therefore, these steps are based on the information provided in passages 1-2.", "response": "Clean the outside portion of the dryer vent by locating the vent cover, removing it, and using a lint brush to clean the inside. Then, remove the vent from the dryer and clean it as well.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 21, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "ground_truth": "The earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, cramping, nausea, and vomiting.", "response": "The earliest signs of pregnancy can include mood swings, dizziness, bloating, spotting, cramping, and nausea and vomiting.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 20}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 92.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 22, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\nPassage 1 states to defrost the roast first and then place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour. After taking it out, season the roast and turn the oven temperature to 350°F. Cook for 1.5 to 3 hours, depending on the size of the roast, making sure it's cooked all the way through.\n\nPassage 2 provides specific instructions for preparing the roast before cooking. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and any desired herbs. Place the roast in a preheated oven at 325°F and determine the cooking time based on the weight of the roast.\n\nPassage 3 suggests starting by preheating the oven to 350°F and then placing the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on a roasting rack. Cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, inserting a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature once cooked. Once the temperature reaches 150°F, remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.\n\nBased on these passages, the general steps to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven are:\n\n1. Defrost the roast if not already thawed.\n2. Season the roast with salt, pepper, and herbs.\n3. Place the roast in a preheated oven at the appropriate temperature (250°F or 325°F) for the specified time.\n4. Check the internal temperature of the roast using a meat thermometer to ensure it reaches the desired doneness.\n5. Remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin roast in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 23, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "ground_truth": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be installed. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater to keep it hot. This continuous loop ensures that hot water is always available.", "response": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This pump circulates the water through the water heater to keep it hot.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 65.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 24, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can i check taxes were filed", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return by:\n\n1. Using the IRS2Go app on your smartphone to check the status of your tax return online.\n2. Checking the status of your tax return over the phone by calling the IRS.\n3. Checking the status of your state tax return online or over the phone.\n\nTo check the status of your tax return, you will need your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, you can check the status 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to check taxes were filed is:\n\nYou can check the status of your tax return online or over the phone using the methods described above.", "response": "You can check the status of a tax return using IRS2Go, an application that allows you to handle taxes online. If you e-filed your taxes, you should be able to get a refund status within 72 hours. If you mail your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.03, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 25, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 26, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that having a bowel movement does not result in weight loss. Weight loss is primarily determined by caloric intake and expenditure, not by bowel movements.", "response": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 27, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "ground_truth": "An ad hominem fallacy occurs when someone attacks the character, motive, or other personal attribute of the person making an argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. This is often done to invalidate their arguments by associating their character with the soundness of their argument. On the other hand, the poisoning the well fallacy, which is a type of ad hominem attack, occurs when a person's integrity or intelligence is attacked before the merits of a case can be considered, effectively redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "response": "The difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is that ad hominem fallacy attacks the argument directly by attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, while poisoning the well fallacy takes place before the merits of a case can be considered and attempts to discredit the argument by attacking the integrity or intelligence of the person.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.3, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.2, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 28, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is dmso used for", "ground_truth": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used in a variety of ways both industrially and medically. Industrially, it is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for numerous chemicals. Medically, DMSO is applied to the skin as an anti-inflammatory and general pain reliever, most commonly for muscles and joints. It is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, and skin ulcers. DMSO has the unique ability to penetrate skin and tissue, allowing it to enter the bloodstream.", "response": "DMSO is used for pain relief, reducing swelling, inflammation, and many other medical ailments. It is also used to promote healing and is applied to the skin to penetrate the tissue and enter the bloodstream.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
