{"id": 30, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\n\nIt is important to note that an instructional video is also available that shows the entire process and location of the screws and pin.", "response": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 31, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do i breed a shugabeats in my singing monsters", "ground_truth": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you need to first obtain a Shugabush monster from the Shugabush Island. Then, hatch the eggs obtained and purchase the breeding structure. Finally, use a Shugabush and a Furcorn in the breeding structure to create a Shugabeats monster.", "response": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you need to obtain the Shugabush Monster from another island, turn it into an egg, hatch it, purchase the breeding structure, and then breed the Shugabush and Furcorn using the Shugabush Island breeding structure.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 73.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 32, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do twins happen", "ground_truth": "Twins can happen in two ways: monozygotic (identical) twins occur when one zygote splits into two embryos, while dizygotic (fraternal) twins happen when two different eggs are fertilized by two separate sperm cells. The likelihood of dizygotic twins is influenced by factors such as West African descent, being between 30 and 40 years old, being taller and heavier than average, and having had several previous pregnancies. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the zygote happens within 8 days of fertilization and can result in complications due to shared organs.", "response": "Twins can happen in two ways: monozygotic (identical) twins and dizygotic (fraternal) twins.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 33, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to find someone in france", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to find someone in France:\n\n1. Check the French White Pages (in English): You can use the website pagesjaunes.fr to search for people in France. To search for someone in Paris or its suburbs, enter \"IDF\" (Ile de France) in the department or region field instead of typing Paris.\n2. Use the nom field to enter the last name of the person you are looking for, and you can also include their first name in the prenom field.\n3. Provide address information, if known, in the ou section to refine your search.\n4. Click \"trouver\" to search for the name, and the search results will display name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.\n\nNote that the effectiveness of these methods may depend on how up-to-date the information in the white pages is and whether the person you are looking for has listed their contact information publicly.", "response": "To find someone in France, you can use a website for people search in France. You can enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field on the website. You can also try sending an email or letter to the town hall in the city of birth.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.99, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 34, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how is a caldera different from a crater", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, a caldera is a large depression made due to volcanic activity, while a volcanic crater is a bowl-like structure at the top of a volcano that allows for the eruption of magma and lava. The primary difference between the two is the method of formation. Calderas are formed when a magma chamber collapses, resulting in a large depression, while craters are formed by impacts from meteorites.", "response": "A caldera is different from a crater in how they are formed. A caldera is a large, circular depression formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, while a crater is caused by impacts from meteorites", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 35, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "ground_truth": "Sure, here are some benefits of hiking as a hobby mentioned in the passages:\n\n* Promotes mental health\n* Increases levels of vitamin D\n* Cardiovascular benefits, such as reducing the risk of heart disease and increasing overall fitness\n* Positive impact on combating symptoms of stress and anxiety\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "Hiking as a hobby has numerous benefits for both the body and the mind. It promotes mental health and reduces stress and anxiety.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 36, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, Snapchat may temporarily lock an account if the user has been using third-party applications to access the app. These third-party apps can compromise the security of the account and put the user and their friends at risk. Snapchat may send a warning message before locking the account, but if the user continues to use third-party apps, their account may be locked.", "response": "Snapchat accounts may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 5.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.09, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 37, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, there are several ways to track who likes your tweets:\n\n1. Favotter.net and Favstar.fm - These websites allow you to track who has favorited your tweets and which tweets have been favorited by multiple users. (Passage 1)\n2. Using a web-based website - There are websites that allow you to check Twitter users who favorite tweets. (Passage 2)\n3. On Twitter - You can set up your account settings to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is: You can use Favotter.net, Favstar.fm, or a web-based website to track who likes your tweets, or you can set up your Twitter account settings to receive email notifications.", "response": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by setting up notifications on your Twitter account to receive email alerts whenever someone favorites one of your tweets.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 38, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 39, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do raffles work", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA raffle is a game of chance where participants buy tickets with a unique number, and a prize is awarded to the holder of the winning ticket drawn at random. In a reverse raffle, the process is similar, but the tickets are numbered from 1 to approximately 55, and tables consist of 20 individuals, constituting one complete ticket at $1000, with two $500 prizes available. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, with 50% going to the winner of the random draw and the remaining 50% going to a charitable cause.\n\nTherefore, raffles typically involve buying tickets with unique numbers, and a random draw determines the winner, with a percentage of the proceeds often going to a charitable cause.", "response": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants with a chance to win prizes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 40, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are mentioned in the following passages:\n\n* Passage 1: In the context of the Greenbriar Boys recording the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" with singer Dian James in 1963.\n* Passage 2: As part of a fragmented repetition of the line \"He was a friend of mine\" in the passage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nPassage 1 and Passage 2", "response": "He was a friend of mine. He died without a penny he didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun he died neath the midnight sun.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 41, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "why does the company Oracle have 2 CEOs", "ground_truth": "Oracle has two CEOs because the former CEO, Larry Ellison, stepped down and chose to have two of his co-presidents, Safra Catz and Mark Hurd, share the role of CEO.", "response": "Oracle has two CEOs to continue its operations and ensure that no single individual holds too much power.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 42, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what do i do if i got my sperrys wet", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, if your Sperry shoes get wet, it is recommended to use a leather conditioner to help revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your shoes with detergent, as it tends to dry out the leather. If you don't have a leather conditioner on hand, you can use a suede bar or leather brush to clean the shoes. It's best to avoid getting light tan Sperry shoes wet, as water might stain them. However, if you do get them wet, using a suede bar or leather brush should help remove any stains.", "response": "If your Sperrys are regular, dark brown ones, you can get them wet without much concern. If they are light tan, water might stain them, but it is unlikely.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 43, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "ground_truth": "To do employee schedules, you need to first understand work laws related to overtime and age restrictions, and you may need to consult a lawyer for this. After that, make a list of all your employees and their duties. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create a chart of work days and hours for each day. Once the schedule is complete, it can be distributed to employees through printing physical copies or sending digital copies to employee email accounts. It's advisable to keep a master schedule in case changes need to be made. Tools like Microsoft Excel can be used to create these schedules, especially as your business grows.", "response": "To create employee schedules, you can use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform, and create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.21, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 44, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "ground_truth": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "response": "Technology has changed the workplace by drastically altering the attitude and processes of the workplace, shifting how we spend our time, and allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work out on the road.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 45, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "ground_truth": "The nervous system and endocrine system have both similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n1. Both systems are dedicated to maintaining homeostasis and coordinating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers play a crucial role in both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while chemical hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system utilizes interconnected cells to transmit signals, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "response": "The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands. Transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses in the nervous system. In contrast, hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the Endocrine System. The nervous system is continuous in which the cells are interconnected. In contrast, the organs of the Endocrine System are not physically connected as they are discrete in nature. The nervous system utilizes the neurons to transmit the signal.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 46, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "ground_truth": "Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are found in the blood and are part of the circulatory system. They are both formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow and contain cell membranes and cytoplasm. The main difference is their functions. RBCs are responsible for delivering oxygen from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases, viruses, etc.", "response": "Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery to the body's tissues, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat diseases. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system, carrying oxygen, whereas white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat diseases.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.19, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 47, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "color of urin meaning", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, we know that red urine can indicate blood in the urine and can potentially be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. On the other hand, deep purple urine is associated with porphyria, a rare genetic disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome, but its color may change due to various factors such as kidney diseases. Therefore, the color of urine can provide important information about one's health and should be monitored closely.", "response": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions, and it can be affected by external factors such as foods and medications.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 48, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can answer your question based on the given passages. Here are some uses for vinegar for dogs:\n\n1. Coat and skin health: Mixing vinegar with water and using it as a final rinse can help to rejuvenate your dog's coat and balance their skin pH levels, according to Passage 1.\n2. Flea control: Vinegar can be used to repel fleas and remove them from your dog's coat, as mentioned in Passage 2.\n3. Itchy ears: Diluted vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears, as stated in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or if there's anything else I can assist you with.", "response": "vinegar can be used to create a shiny, healthy coat, normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin, soothe itchy ears, and repel fleas.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 49, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "inventory costing weighted average", "ground_truth": "The weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each item of inventory when it is sold. This is calculated by taking the average cost of all inventories currently available. This cost fluctuates as inventory prices change. The weighted average cost per unit is determined by dividing the cost of goods available for sale by the number of units available for sale. This cost is then assigned to both ending inventory and the cost of goods sold. This method is often used when it's impossible to assign specific costs to individual units or when the accounting system isn't sophisticated enough to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers. The recorded amount of inventory on hand using this method represents a value between the oldest and newest units purchased into stock.", "response": "The weighted average method of costing inventory assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. When a unit of inventory is sold, the weighted average method of costing inventory takes the average cost of all inventories currently available. This average price is then assigned to the item sold. Since inventory prices fluctuate, the weighted average cost will also change.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
