{"id": 53, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "weather in wellesley", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the weather in Wellesley for Tuesday, August 23rd is expected to be sunny with a high of 82 degrees and a 39% chance of rain. The wind speed is expected to be 10 mph from the north-northwest.", "response": "The weather in Wellesley on Aug 23 is forecasted to be 82 degrees and Sunny with a 39 percentage chance of rain and 10 mph winds from the North-Northwest.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.47, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 54, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "ground_truth": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nThe main difference between SMS (Short Message Service) and MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is that SMS is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows for sending multimedia content such as images, videos, and audio files, in addition to text.\n\nAccording to passage 1, SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts if they are longer. MMS messages, on the other hand, can carry a larger size of content, including pictures, videos, and audio files, with a maximum size of 300KB.\n\nPassage 2 explains that SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies, while passage 3 highlights the differences between SMS and MMS, stating that SMS only allows for text, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\n\n* SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n* SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts, while MMS messages can carry a larger size of content.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "response": "SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, or any combination of these.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "ground_truth": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services. They administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The site is also for providers, offering them resources like weekly Q&A sessions each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. where they can address their questions and issues. Additionally, they offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses, approved by organizations like the American Psychological Association and the Association of Social Work Boards.", "response": "Magellan of Virginia is a company that administers behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs and hosts provider Q&A sessions on Fridays.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a possible solution to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check if the door stops are properly aligned. If the door stops are not aligned, use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose. Remove the door stop and use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb and set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n2. Check if the latch hole in the jamb is properly aligned with the strike plate. If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, tighten the hinges first. Then, enlarge the strike plate hole. Move the strike plate if necessary.\n\nIf these steps do not solve the problem, it may be necessary to seek further assistance from a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "response": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try shutting the door and trying to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 2, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first, run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Next, apply nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth and then mix liquid laundry soap with water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "response": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, you can use a regular dryer setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth, then mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water and dip a clean cloth in this solution to rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 75.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 3, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "ground_truth": "A water pick, also known as a Waterpik, is a beneficial tool for oral care. It is designed to shoot a strong stream of water at the gum line to help eliminate germs and plaque that are tough to get rid of with a toothbrush. It can also help maintain overall body health. In comparison to flossing, using a water pick can be easier and leave your mouth feeling cleaner. It can also massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis. It is especially useful in cleaning around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing cannot reach.", "response": "gums, mouth, and overall body healthier. It shoots a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque that are difficult to remove with a toothbrush. It is useful in maintaining good oral health by massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth, which helps reduce the risk of gingivitis. It helps to clean better around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing cannot access.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.25, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 4, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun (Passage 1:4). This will prevent birds from reaching the areas they often choose to build their nests.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it (Passage 2:1). Choose a non-flammable netting that is safe to use around light bulbs, and ensure that it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds from the area (Passage 3:1). Move the plastic hawk periodically to avoid the birds becoming accustomed to it.\n\nPlease note that the effectiveness of these methods may vary depending on the type of birds and the location of your porch. If the above methods do not work, you may need to consider other solutions or consult with a professional for assistance.", "response": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 19}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 5, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you:\n\n1. Physical contact: Avoid physical contact that could be misinterpreted as fondling or sexual activity (Passage 1).\n2. Eye contact: If your coworker is consistently staring at you, it may be a sign that they are interested in you (Passage 2).\n3. Smiling: If your coworker smiles at you excessively, even when there is no apparent reason to do so, it may be a sign of flirtation (Passage 2).\n4. Seeking contact: If your coworker consistently finds reasons to be near you or seek you out discreetly, it may indicate that they have feelings for you (Passage 3).\n\nHowever, it is essential to remember that these signs alone do not necessarily mean that your coworker is interested in you romantically. It's important to pay attention to the context of their behavior and communicate openly to avoid misunderstandings.\n\nIf you are unsure about your coworker's intentions, it may be best to avoid physical contact and observe their behavior over time before making any conclusions. Additionally, it's crucial to respect your coworker's boundaries and maintain a professional work environment.", "response": "If your male coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests you not continue flirting with him, it is a sign that he is not interested. Additionally, if the coworker finds any reason to touch you, it is a sign of flirting.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 6, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the symptoms and causes of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) based on the given passages:\n\nSymptoms:\n\n* Diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea)\n* Constipation\n* Constipation alternating with diarrhea\n* Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement\n* A lot of gas or bloating\n\nCauses:\n\n* Abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements\n* Increased awareness of bodily functions\n* Disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract\n* Alterations in the GI tract motility\n* Abnormal nervous system signals\n* Increased sensitivity to pain\n* Food intolerances\n* Poor absorption of sugars or acids in food\n\nIt's worth noting that the exact cause of IBS is still unknown, and it's believed to be a complex interaction of various factors.", "response": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, alternating diarrhea and constipation, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of IBS include abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 7, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between essential and nonessential amino acids", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between essential and non-essential amino acids are:\n\nEssential Amino Acids:\n\n* Must be obtained from the diet\n* Cannot be produced by the body\n* Nine out of 20 amino acids are considered essential (valine, isoleucine, leucine, lysine, methionine, phenylalanine, threonine, tryptophan, and histidine for infants)\n\nNon-Essential Amino Acids:\n\n* Can be produced by the body\n* Not necessarily required to obtain from the diet\n* Include alanine, asparagine, aspartic acid, glutamic acid, arginine, cysteine, glutamine, glycine, ornithine, proline, serine, and tyrosine\n\nIt is important to note that even though non-essential amino acids can be produced by the body, it is still important to consume a balanced diet that includes all of the essential amino acids to ensure proper bodily functions.", "response": "Essential amino acids are those that cannot be synthesized by the body and must be obtained from dietary sources, while nonessential amino acids can be synthesized by the body from essential amino acids or by breaking down protein products.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 8, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how the body systems work together", "ground_truth": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "response": "The body systems work together by each system performing its specific function, while also supporting and interacting with other systems to maintain overall body function. For example, the urinary system cleans", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 7.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 18}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.34, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 9, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "ground_truth": "To transfer water shares, the seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of it. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. After these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner. If the original certificate is lost, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.", "response": "Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller, providing proof of ownership, and paying a fee of $75.00.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 10, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "teresa name meaning", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the meaning of the name Teresa is:\n\n* Reap; from Therasia (Greek)\n* Reaper; from Therasia (American)\n* Harvester (Italian)\n* Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux' (Spanish)\n\nIt is also mentioned that the name Teresa is a Greek baby name, an American baby name, an Italian baby name, and a Spanish baby name.\n\nTherefore, the meaning of the name Teresa can vary depending on the culture and language, but it generally means \"reaper\" or \"harvester\", and is also associated with the names of two popular saints.", "response": "Reap; from Therasia", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 9.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 11, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "ground_truth": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the cloves intact. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up, and drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, rubbing it over the cloves. Roast the cloves in the preheated oven for about 45 minutes to an hour, or until they are softened. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 12, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 13, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "show me how can i make gragh for my research", "ground_truth": "To create a graph for your research, you first need to collect all of your data, remembering that the graph should show a comparison among categories. If you are creating a bar graph, you will use rectangular bars to represent different values. You need to title your graph and determine how high your graph needs to go. If your data points are substantially different in scale, you can use a pie chart. The y-axis of your graph will have a scale, and each bar’s height should be proportionate to the size of the category it represents. Make sure to consider any disproportionate responses that might impact the scale of your graph. Regardless of the type of graph you choose, it should provide a clear visual representation of your information.", "response": "To make a graph for your research, you can use a bar graph or a line graph. Bar graphs are used to compare groups or types and give great visual representation of information. To make a bar graph, you'll need to title it and find out how high your graph needs to go.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 14, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "ground_truth": "Hugging has physiological benefits and can have a similar effect on the body as certain drugs. It can also lead to emotional intimacy and happy relationships. Hugging and touch, even with inanimate objects, can help reduce existential fears and worry about mortality.", "response": "Psychological effects of hugging include leading to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages, and reducing existential fears.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.82, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 15, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo attach multiple picture frames together, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\n5. Repeat the process for additional frames, ensuring that the hinge placement is consistent across all frames.\n6. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the grouped frames and hang them up.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: Select frames with the same wood molding, lay them together, mark hinge placement, attach hinges, and attach a hanging wire to the back.", "response": "To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for two frames and choose three of the same or one larger frame for three frames. Mark the hinge placement the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.05, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 16, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot and is characterized by its large, fleshy leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a stronger, more assertive flavor than spinach and can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri. Chard is a beet that has been selected for leaf production rather than storage root formation and can be harvested when young and tender or after maturity. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden, but it is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a maximum of 2-3 days.", "response": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 17, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to peel potatoes fast", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Boil the potatoes for about 15 minutes.\n3. Place the potatoes in a bowl of ice water and swish them around for a few seconds.\n4. Remove the potatoes from the water and remove the skin.\n\nAlternatively, you can also try the following method:\n\n1. Cut the potato skin, making a cut all around the potato lengthwise.\n2. Boil the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds.\n4. Rub the potato with both hands, and the skin should fall right off.\n\nThese methods should help you peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "response": "Score the potatoes all the way around with a knife, boil them for about 15 minutes, plunge them into ice water for 10 seconds, and then remove the skin by rubbing the potato with both hands.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.19, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 18, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "average weather sausalito", "ground_truth": "Average weather in Sausalito can vary depending on the time of year. For example, during September, the average temperature is 58 degrees Fahrenheit (15 degrees Celsius), while in January, it is only 43 degrees Fahrenheit (4 degrees Celsius). The most precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches. However, throughout the year, the number of days with measurable precipitation is 56, and there are an average of 256 sunny days.", "response": "Average weather in Sausalito is relatively mild with an average monthly temperature of around 58 degrees in September and 50 degrees in December. The highest monthly average temperature is around 69 degrees in July, while the lowest monthly average temperature is around 43 degrees in January. The most monthly precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches, and the average annual precipitation is 34 inches, which is less than the US average of 39 inches. Snowfall is negligible, with only 0 inches in Sausalito, compared to the US average of 26 inches. The number of days with any measurable precipitation is 56, and there are 256 sunny days per year", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 19, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "response": "The FEHA and ADA differ in their scope", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.02, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 20, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "ground_truth": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean dryer vent\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo clean the dryer vent, start by locating the vent cover on the outside of the house and removing it. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer and use a dryer vent brush to clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning the area around the lint filter for a more thorough cleaning. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits and ensure your dryer runs efficiently.\n\nIf the passages did not contain the necessary information to answer the question, I would have replied with \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "response": "Clean the outside portion of the dryer vent by locating the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house, removing the cover, and using a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole. Next, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 21, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "ground_truth": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition characterized by significant bone density loss, resulting in weakened bones and increased risk of fractures. Symptoms may include sudden and severe back pain, loss of height over time, fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, fractures, particularly in the spine or hips, are likely to occur.", "response": "Severe osteoporosis is a condition that has virtually no symptoms until severe bone damage has already occurred. It can cause symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with stooped posture, fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 22, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Defrost the pork loin if possible. If you don't have time to defrost, you can place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour.\n2. Preheat the oven to 325°F (passage 2).\n3. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with 2 tsp of olive oil and season the outside with salt, pepper, and desired herbs (thyme, oregano, or garlic work well) (passage 2).\n4. Place the pork loin in a roasting pan and put it in the preheated oven (passage 2).\n5. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 150°F (passage 3).\n6. Use a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature of the meat (passage 3).\n7. Once the meat is cooked, remove it from the oven and cover it with aluminum foil for 30 minutes before serving (passage 3).\n\nNote that the exact cooking time may vary depending on the size of the roast, so adjust the cooking time accordingly. Also, make sure to check the internal temperature of the meat to ensure that it is cooked all the way through.", "response": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 23, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "ground_truth": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "response": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 24, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the effect of a carbon footprint is a measure of the negative impact of human activities on the environment. The measurement of a carbon footprint typically indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced through daily activities. Additionally, reducing one's carbon footprint can have a positive impact on the environment, even if the changes may seem small.", "response": "The effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of one's lifestyle. It indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced as a result of daily activities.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 25, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "response": "Use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 26, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the answer is: No, having a bowel movement does not cause weight loss. The passages state that body weight loss comes from creating a calorie deficit, not from losing body fat in stools. Additionally, the fat in stools is not derived from body fat, but rather from dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed. Therefore, hopping on the bathroom scale before and after a bowel movement will not accurately reflect any weight loss due to the bowel movement itself.", "response": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 27, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is that ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. On the other hand, poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, specifically attacking a person's integrity or intelligence to redirect the discussion towards their faults.", "response": "Ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy involves attacking the faults of one of the parties before the merits of a case can be considered.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 28, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is dmso used for", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various purposes, including:\n\n1. Industrial uses: As an antifreeze and solvent for a wide range of chemicals.\n2. Medical uses: To relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, promote healing, and treat a variety of medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and soft tissue damage.\n3. Pain relief: For muscles and joints, and as a general pain reliever applied to the skin.\n4. Skin care: To penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is DMSO used for?\" can be summarized as: DMSO is used for various industrial, medical, and personal care purposes, including pain relief, wound healing, and skin care.", "response": "DMSO is used for pain relief, reducing swelling and inflammation, promoting healing, and as an anti-inflammatory.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 29, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "why should we serve others", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"Why should we serve others?\"\n\nWe should serve others because it is a way to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who may not treat us well. Serving others is an expression of our love for God and our desire to be like Him. When we truly know God, our natural response is a desire to love and serve Him in return, and serving others is a way to do so. Additionally, serving others without self-serving motives and expecting nothing in return allows us to serve out of love and build stronger character muscles.\n\nTherefore, serving others is not only a way to show love and kindness, but it is also a way to deepen our relationship with God and grow in our faith.", "response": "Serving others is a crucial part of the Christian life, as it is a way to show love and kindness to everyone, even to those who do not treat us well. It is also a way to build and strengthen our character muscles and to receive greater rewards than if we were to serve with self-serving motives.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 30, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n\nAfter removing the screws and clips, you will be able to remove the door panel. It is recommended to watch an instructional video to see the process and locate the parts mentioned.", "response": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin the holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 31, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do i breed a shugabeats in my singing monsters", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's what we know about breeding a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters:\n\n* We need to breed a Shugabush Monster with a Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure to get a Shugabeats.\n* The breeding combination for Shugabeats is Shugabush + Furcorn.\n* Breeding left or right does not matter.\n\nTherefore, to breed a Shugabeats, you need to have a Shugabush Monster and a Furcorn, and then breed them together in the Shugabush Island breeding structure.\n\nAnswer: Breed a Shugabush Monster and a Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure.", "response": "To breed a Shugabeats in My Singing Monsters, you need to obtain the Shugabush Monster from another island, turn the Shugabush Monsters into eggs, hatch them, buy the breeding structure, and then breed using the Shugabush and the Furcorn in the Shugabush Island breeding structure.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.3, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 32, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do twins happen", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how twins happen:\n\n* Monoamniotic twins: These twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization.\n* Conjoined twins: When the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs, it happens within 8 days of fertilization, and mortality is highest for conjoined twins due to the many complications resulting from shared organs.\n* Dizygotic twin pregnancies: These twins are slightly more likely to occur in women who are of West African descent (especially Yoruba), between the ages of 30 and 40, are taller and heavier than average, and have had several previous pregnancies.\n* Identical twins (monozygotic): These twins develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos.\n* Fraternal twins (dizygotic): These twins develop from two different eggs, and each twin is fertilized by its own sperm cell.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages: The passage does not provide information on the exact timing or mechanism of twinning beyond what is mentioned above.", "response": "Twins can happen either when a single zygote splits into two embryos (monozygotic twins) or when two different eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells (dizygotic twins).", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 33, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to find someone in france", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to find someone in France:\n\n1. Use a people search website specifically designed for France, such as People Search France.\n2. Check the French white pages (in English) at PagesJaunes.fr. Instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field to search for the person in Paris and its suburbs.\n3. Post a missed connection (MC) on Paris Craigslist.\n4. Visit the Pages Blanches (the French version of the white pages) at PagesJaunes.fr. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field, and optionally enter a first name in the Prenom field. Enter address information, if known, in the Ou section. Click Trouver to search for the name. The search results will display name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.", "response": "To find someone in France, you can try using the French white pages (in English) by visiting the website www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field. The French white pages will display name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.59, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 34, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how the colonists respond to the stamp act. why was it so upsetting?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the colonists responded to the Stamp Act of 1765 with a mix of violent and non-violent protests. They held peaceful protests, chanting slogans such as \"No Taxation without Representation,\" but these were often met with violence from British soldiers, known as Red Coats, who would come to cause fights and make arrests. The colonists also organized public protests, legislative resolutions, town meetings, and boycotts of British goods throughout the colonies. The Stamp Act was seen as particularly egregious because it was the first direct tax imposed by Parliament on the colonies, and it required the use of tax-stamped paper for all newspapers, legal documents, and other printed materials. The colonists felt that this was an overreach of British authority and a violation of their rights as British subjects. The Act was eventually repealed in 1766, but it had already sparked widespread outrage and resistance among the colonists, contributing to the growing tensions that would eventually lead to the American Revolution.", "response": "The colonists responded to the Stamp Act with a combination of peaceful and non-violent methods, including public protests, legislative resolutions, town meetings, and citizen boycotts of British goods. The Stamp Act was particularly upsetting because it imposed a direct tax on the colonists, which they saw as a violation of their rights.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 35, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "ground_truth": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, has no discernible taste or smell, and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.", "response": "Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of the fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Unrefined coconut oil has a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil has no discernible taste or smell. Refined coconut oil has a smoking point of 450 degrees F, whereas the smoking point of unrefined coconut oil is 350 degrees F. Because of its greater heat tolerance, refined coconut oil can be a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 65.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 36, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it appears that Snapchat may lock accounts that use third-party applications to access the platform more than four times. If a user has been locked out of their account and doesn't know why, using third-party apps may be a reason. Third-party apps are applications that are not developed or officially supported by Snapchat, such as third-party messaging or camera apps. Using these apps may put the user's account at risk, as well as their friends'. Additionally, there are many reasons why people are getting locked out of Snapchat, including using third-party apps.", "response": "Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you were using a third-party application to access Snapchat, which is not secure and can put you and your friends at risk.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 37, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can tell who liked your tweet:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm to track who has favorited your tweets. These websites show you a list of users who have favorited your tweets, allowing you to see who has shown interest in your content.\n\nPassage 2 provides a step-by-step guide on how to track who favorited your tweets. According to the passage, you can use a simple web-based website to check who favorited your tweets. Once you have access to this website, you can enter your tweet's URL to view a list of users who have favorited it.\n\nPassage 3 does not provide any information on tracking who favorited your tweets. However, it does mention that you can set up your Twitter account to notify you via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\n\nIn summary, to tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or set up your Twitter account to notify you via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "response": "To tell who liked your tweet, go to Twitter.com and log in with your Twitter username and password. Click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page. Click on the Settings option", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 38, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "ground_truth": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "response": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks, leading to a corresponding price difference.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 39, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "temperature for tallahassee florida", "ground_truth": "Tallahassee, Florida has an overall average high temperature of 79 degrees and an average low of 56 degrees. Freezing temperatures can sporadically occur from November to March, with two or three nights on average even dropping to 20 °F or lower.", "response": "The temperature for Tallahassee, Florida varies throughout the year, with an overall average high of 79 degrees and an average low of 56 degrees.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 40, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are from the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" written by Bob Dylan.", "response": "He was a friend of mine he was a friend of mine. He died without a penny\nhe didn't have a dime he was a friend of mine. He died neath the midnight sun\nhe died neath the midnight sun.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 41, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "global egalitarianism meaning", "ground_truth": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the three provided passages:\n\nGlobal egalitarianism refers to the idea that all individuals should have equal rights and opportunities regardless of their background, location, or culture. However, the passages suggest that achieving global egalitarianism is challenging due to difficulties in measuring resources and opportunities across different cultures. Additionally, the passages hint that there may be different types of egalitarianism, such as instrumental and non-instrumental, but do not provide further explanation or clarification. Therefore, without more information, it is difficult to give a more specific definition of global egalitarianism based solely on these passages.", "response": "Global egalitarianism is a concept that measures and evaluates the distribution of resources and opportunities among people across different societies. It is a principle of global justice that seeks to ensure fairness and equality for all individuals, regardless of their cultural background", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 42, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "where does 1099-patr go on 1040", "ground_truth": "Per the IRS instructions, patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1,2,3, and 5 from a cooperative, which are reported in Form 1099-PATR, are reported on Schedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835 of the Form 1040.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 43, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "ground_truth": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "response": "To create employee schedules, make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform, make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day, use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create the schedule, print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts, keep a master schedule for to make any changes, and if you are using Microsoft Excel, use it to create a work schedule for multiple employees so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 72.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 44, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including:\n\n1. Increased efficiency and productivity: Technology has enabled automation of many tasks, allowing employees to focus on more complex and creative work, leading to increased productivity.\n2. Changes in workplace dynamics: Technology has transformed the way people communicate and collaborate in the workplace, enabling remote work and virtual teams.\n3. Rapid advancements: Technology has rapidly advanced in recent years, allowing employees to access new tools and resources, and adapt to changing market conditions.\n4. Global connectivity: Technology has enabled employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, allowing for greater flexibility and mobility.\n\nTherefore, technology has had a significant impact on the modern workplace, transforming the way people work, communicate, and collaborate.", "response": "Technology has changed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, altering the dynamics of the workplace, and enabling global interaction.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 45, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the nervous system and endocrine system have some similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n- Both systems are responsible for maintaining homeostasis in the body.\n- Both systems use chemical messengers to coordinate and regulate the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n- Negative feedback mechanisms are used to regulate both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n- The nervous system is made up of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses while transmission in the endocrine system is done through chemicals called hormones.\n- The nervous system is a continuous network of interconnected cells while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs that are not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "response": "The nervous system is made of neuron cells and transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses, while the endocrine system is made of glands and transmission is performed by chemicals known as hormones. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected, being discrete in nature. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, and the circulatory system is used by the endocrine system to transmit signals. Both the nervous and endocrine systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs in the two systems.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 70.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 46, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the primary difference between red and white blood cells is their respective functions within the body. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery to tissues, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat diseases and viruses. However, both types of cells share some common features, such as being formed elements of blood, being formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow, having a cell membrane and cytoplasm, and circulating in the fluids in blood vessels, which is pumped by the heart.", "response": "Red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are both formed from stem cells in the red bone marrow, have cell membranes and cytoplasm, and are found in the circulatory system. However, RBCs are responsible for oxygen delivery and are not involved in immune response, while WBCs are part of the immune system and combat diseases and viruses.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 47, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "color of urin meaning", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the color of urine can indicate various things, including:\n\n* Blood in the urine (passage 1)\n* Porphyria (a rare inherited disorder) (passage 2)\n* Kidney diseases (passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What does the color of urine mean?\" is:\n\nAnswer: Depending on the passage, the color of urine can indicate different things, such as blood, porphyria, or kidney diseases.", "response": "Pale yellow", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 48, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "ground_truth": "Sure, here are some possible answers based on the given passages:\n\nQ: What are some uses for vinegar when it comes to dogs?\n\nA: Vinegar can be used to:\n\n* Improve a dog's skin and coat by mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and using it as a final rinse.\n* Normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin by spraying full-strength vinegar on its coat.\n* Repel fleas by spraying a dog's coat with apple cider vinegar.\n* Soothe itchy ears by using a diluted solution of apple cider vinegar (50% water, 50% vinegar) on a cotton swab or gauze pad.\n* Clean a dog's ears by using apple cider vinegar.\n* Fight fleas by bathing a dog in a soap mixture that includes apple cider vinegar.\n* Remove fleas using a flea comb after bathing a dog in an apple cider vinegar soap mixture.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "response": "vinegar can be used to rejuvenate a dog's coat, balance its skin pH levels, improve the dog's skin and coat, clean out the dog's ears, repel fleas, fight fleas, rinse the dog, and soothe itchy ears.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 49, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "inventory costing weighted average", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it can be understood that the Weighted Average Costing (WAC) method is used to determine the average cost of inventory when a unit is sold. This method takes the average cost of all inventories currently available and uses it to calculate the weighted average cost per unit. WAC is commonly used when inventory items are intermingled and it's difficult to assign a specific cost to an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sophisticated enough to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers.", "response": "The weighted average method of costing inventory assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. When a unit of inventory is sold, the weighted average method of costing inventory takes the average cost of all inventories currently available. This average price is then assigned to the item sold. Since inventory prices fluctuate, the weighted average cost will also change.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 50, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "michigan-how much to replace sewer lines", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe passages provided do not contain specific information about the cost of replacing sewer lines in Michigan or any other location. Passage 2 mentions general cost ranges for sewer line repair and replacement, but these costs are not specific to Michigan and may vary depending on various factors such as location, materials, and labor costs. Passage 3 is a call to action to ask a question on Angie's List, but does not provide any information relevant to the question at hand. Therefore, I cannot provide an answer to the question based on the given passages.", "response": "$3,000 to around $12,000", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 51, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved, then heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2).\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2).\n4. Once the ice cream base is ready, pour it into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\n\nNote that the passages do not provide a specific recipe for making ice cream, but rather provide general steps and tips for making ice cream using an ice cream maker.", "response": "To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen, 2 to 3 hours.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.02, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 52, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what exercises tone the chest", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the exercises that tone the chest are:\n\n1. Modified tri-set for the chest (mentioned in passage 2)\n2. Pushups with heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses (mentioned in passage 2)\n\nThese exercises are designed to pump the pecs and stretch the connective tissue surrounding them, allowing for more muscle growth.", "response": "Lay on your back with a dumbbell in each hand. Extend your arms out to your side, as if you were forming a cross. Slowly, with your arms still extended, curl your hands together until the dumbbells meet above the center of your chest. Slowly return your arms back to your sides.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 53, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "ground_truth": "The process of air reaching the lungs involves the diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing. When the diaphragm contracts, it moves down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region, allowing air to enter the lungs. This is part of the ventilation component of breathing, which is the movement of oxygen into, and carbon dioxide out of the lungs. Additionally, increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity pulls the lungs along with it, increasing their volume and causing a decrease in air pressure. This forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation.", "response": "The diaphragm muscle contracts to bring air into the lungs and relaxes to let air out.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "ground_truth": "Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure the delivery of quality behavioral health services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and work towards improving the overall health and well-being of Virginians. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly Q&A sessions for providers to address their questions and issues.", "response": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.03, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "ground_truth": "To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper and place them on the baking sheet. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes. If desired, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet and return fish to the oven to allow cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "response": "Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, and bake in a preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 2, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. (Passage 1)\n2. Heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. Once heated, use a cloth to peel off the plastic. (Passage 2)\n3. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and use it to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element after leaving it on the element for 5 minutes. Then, wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth and remove any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to remove plastic from the drum of a clothes dryer.", "response": "To remove plastic from a dryer, you can use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. You can also mix 1 tsp of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 3, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "ground_truth": "A water pick has several benefits, according to the given passages. It can help eliminate germs and plaque that are difficult to remove with a toothbrush. It can also massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis. Additionally, a water pick can clean better around the teeth and gums, reaching areas that brushing may not be able to access.", "response": "The benefits of a water pick include eliminating germs", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 4, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building a nest on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to keep birds from building a nest on your porch is:\n\nAttach bird netting to the eaves or install bird netting over the light fixture, and/or mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "response": "Attach bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun. If your porch has open rafters, use the staple gun to attach the netting to the top of the porch. The netting keeps the birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 22}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 5, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are some signs that a male coworker may be flirting with you:\n\n* He finds reasons to be near you and seek you out discreetly (Passage 3)\n* He is always staring at you and catches your eye (Passage 2)\n* He touches you unnecessarily or finds excuses to have physical contact with you (Passage 2)\n* He smiles at you excessively or without apparent reason (Passage 2)\n* He seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him (Passage 1)\n\nIf you observe these behaviors from a male coworker, it may be a sign that he is interested in you and flirting with you. However, it's essential to remember that these signs alone do not necessarily mean the person likes you romantically, and it's possible they just have a friendly interest in you. To confirm their intentions, consider observing their behavior over time, and if you feel comfortable, try initiating a conversation or asking them out.", "response": "If your male coworker frequently stares at you or smiles at you without a clear reason, it could be a sign that he is flirting with you.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 6, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "ground_truth": "To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end. Then, take another clean slide and holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry and label clearly. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers. Always avoid coming into contact with another person's blood and if it is unavoidable, wear rubber gloves.", "response": "Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface, add one small drop of blood to one end, take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action, push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood, make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place in the provided slide transport containers.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 80.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 7, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between essential and nonessential amino acids", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nEssential amino acids are those that cannot be produced by the body and must be obtained from the diet, while nonessential amino acids are those that can be produced by the body from other amino acids or by breaking down protein products.\n\nPassage 1 states that nine amino acids are essential for humans, but only eight of them are essential for adults (histidine is only essential for infants). Passage 2 explains that nonessential amino acids are not unnecessary, as the body can produce them from essential amino acids or by breaking down protein products. Passage 3 reiterates that nonessential amino acids can be made by the body, while essential amino acids cannot be produced and must be obtained from the diet.\n\nTherefore, the main difference between essential and nonessential amino acids is that essential amino acids cannot be produced by the body and must be obtained from the diet, while nonessential amino acids can be produced by the body from other amino acids or by breaking down protein products.", "response": "Essential amino acids are those that your body cannot produce and must be obtained from your diet, while nonessential amino acids are those that your body can produce, either from essential amino acids or by breaking down protein products.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 8, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how the body systems work together", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here's how the body systems work together:\n\n1. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and nervous systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. (Passage 1)\n2. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood from the body and remove waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. (Passage 2)\n3. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the body systems work together in the following ways:\n\n* The skeletal system provides support and structure for the body, while the muscular system helps move the body and its parts.\n* The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for energy production.\n* The circulatory system delivers oxygenated blood to the body's cells and removes carbon dioxide, while the urinary system removes waste products from the blood.\n* The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, metabolism, and reproductive processes.\n* The lymphatic system helps defend the body against infection and disease, while the immune system fights off foreign invaders.\n* The nervous system controls and coordinates the body's functions, including movement, sensation, and thought processes.\n\nOverall, the body's systems work together in a complex interplay to maintain homeostasis and ensure the proper functioning of the body.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 7.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 9, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "ground_truth": "Water shares are transferred by following a set of steps. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. After completing these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "response": "The process of transferring water shares involves several steps. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. Additionally, a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 71.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 10, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "ground_truth": "To build a lean-to shed, start by preparing the site with a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4\" and set and level them according to the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". Assemble the floor and place it on the skids as indicated in the floor framing section of the plans. Check for squareness and anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Cut two more 4 x 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids and, when the frame is square, toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. The size of the shed can be adjusted as needed.", "response": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel, cutting the two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4″, setting and leveling the skids, cutting two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 ” and six joists at 44 3/4″, and assembling the floor and setting it on the skids.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 11, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "ground_truth": "Here are brief answers to the question on how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nPassage 1: The passage does not provide information on how to roast individual garlic cloves specifically. However, it does mention that larger garlic cloves may take up to an hour to soften when roasted, so it is possible to assume that smaller cloves will take less time.\n\nPassage 2: This passage provides some options for seasoning the garlic before roasting, but it does not provide instructions on how to roast individual garlic cloves.\n\nPassage 3: This passage provides a method for roasting entire garlic heads, but it does not address how to roast individual garlic cloves. The passage does mention that cutting the top of the garlic bulb and exposing the individual cloves can help them roast more evenly, but it does not provide specific instructions on how to do this.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 15.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 12, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "To sew a zipper gusset, first, trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 13, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "show me how can i make gragh for my research", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to create a bar graph for your research:\n\n1. Collect your data: The first step is to gather all the data you want to represent in your graph. Make sure the data is organized and easy to compare.\n2. Decide on the x-axis and y-axis: The x-axis typically represents the category or group being compared, while the y-axis represents the value or amount of each category.\n3. Determine the height of the graph: The height of the graph will depend on the highest value in your data set. Make sure to choose a height that allows for clear representation of all the data points.\n4. Create the bars: Use rectangular bars to represent each category, making sure the height of each bar is proportional to the value it represents.\n5. Add labels and titles: Label each bar with its corresponding category and add a title to the graph that describes the data being represented.\n6. Consider using a pie chart: If you have only a few data points to display and each one is substantially different in scale, a pie chart might be a better option.\n7. Format and refine: Make sure the graph is visually appealing and easy to read. Adjust the scaling of the y-axis if needed, and consider adding colors or shading to make the graph more engaging.\n\nBy following these steps, you should be able to create a clear and effective bar graph for your research. Good luck!", "response": "To make a graph for your research, you can follow these steps: 1. Title the graph and determine how high it needs to go.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 14, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the physiological effects of hugging are numerous and significant. Hugs affect the entire body and can potentially be compared to the effects of multiple drugs operating at once. Furthermore, the act of hugging can also have psychological effects. Empathic listening can lead to emotional intimacy and happy relationships, as well as making conversation partners feel like they are receiving a hug, which can provide comfort and ease their existential fears. Overall, the psychological effects of hugging are positive and suggest that this simple gesture can have a significant impact on our emotional and physical wellbeing.", "response": "Psychological effects of hugging include reducing existential fears, promoting emotional intimacy, and fostering good relationships. Hugs can also be perceived as psychological hugs through empathic listening.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.91, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 15, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "leasing meaning", "ground_truth": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "response": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of certain fixed assets for a series of contractual, periodic, tax-deductible payments.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 16, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "ground_truth": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, meaning all the atoms in an element have the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other. Mixtures have variable compositions and show the properties of their constituent substances. Elements and compounds just mix together to form a mixture and no new compound is formed.", "response": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance composed of only one type of atom, they cannot be separated by physical means. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are pure substances, they can be separated", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 17, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "response": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 18, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "average weather sausalito", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\n\n* Temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 50°F (December) to 58°F (September).\n* Precipitation: Sausalito receives an average of 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January (0 inches).\n* Air Quality Index: The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, but the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average.\n* Sunshine: Sausalito experiences 256 sunny days per year, with an average of 56 days with measurable precipitation.\n* Comfort Index: According to Sperling's comfort index, Sausalito has a score of 84 out of 100, indicating a comfortable year-round climate.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages regarding the average weather in Sausalito during a specific month or time period.", "response": "The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by a high monthly average temperature of 58 degrees in September and a low monthly average temperature of 50 degrees in December. The July high is around 69 degrees, and the January low is 43 degrees. The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 19, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "ground_truth": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, start by preheating an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow to stand for 10 minutes. Finally, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "response": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 5.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 74.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 20, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "the benefits of msm powder", "ground_truth": "MSM powder offers several benefits. It helps get oxygen into the blood more efficiently, thereby increasing energy levels. It also makes cell walls more permeable. The powder aids in the absorption of more nutrients, particularly when paired with Co-enzyme Q10. Additionally, MSM powder can help relieve muscular aches and pains and reduce inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "response": "MSM powder benefits the body by helping absorb more nutrients (vitamins and minerals), increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable, reducing inflammation and swelling, and helping relieve muscular aches and pains.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.95, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 21, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a condition where the bones have been significantly weakened to the point of causing symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures. According to passage 3, osteoporosis typically has no symptoms until significant bone damage has occurred, making it a \"silent disease\" until it reaches this advanced stage. Passage 2 also highlights that compression fractures of the spine are a common cause of osteoporosis pain, which can be severe and debilitating. Therefore, severe osteoporosis is characterized by a high risk of fractures, particularly in the spine and hips, as well as persistent back pain and loss of height.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.13, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 22, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\n\nSo, the steps to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven are: preheat the oven, place the roast in a shallow baking pan, cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, check the internal temperature, cover and let it sit before serving.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 23, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here's how you can make a hot water heater circulate:\n\n1. Install a recirculating pump: As described in passage 3, a recirculating pump can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\n2. Use a demand-based system: According to passage 3, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor. This means that the pump will only run when there is a demand for hot water, rather than constantly running.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to make a hot water heater circulate, but rather describe the concept of circulation and the different types of systems used to achieve it.", "response": "A hot water heater can be made to circulate by using a pump, such as a hot water circulation pump or a recirculating pump. These pumps send cool water back to the water heater through a return line, ensuring that hot water is always available.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 24, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of an individual's lifestyle and daily activities, specifically the amount of greenhouse gases produced, such as carbon dioxide, as a result of those activities. The carbon footprint is typically measured in tons of CO2 released into the atmosphere. The passages also mention that reducing one's carbon footprint can have a significant impact on the environment, even with seemingly small changes. Additionally, the average carbon footprint is mentioned to be around 6 tons per year, with a higher amount in the US due to automobile emissions.", "response": "The effect of carbon footprint is the measurement of the environmental impact of various human activities, quantified by the total amount of greenhouse gases produced within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.3, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 25, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check your dog's body thoroughly, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, around the eyes, and other favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if needed.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily, making sure not to yank it away from your dog too quickly.\n4. Regularly use tick control products on your dog, as recommended by your veterinarian, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the first place.\n\nIf you have any further questions or concerns, consult your veterinarian for advice.", "response": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 26, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"When you have a bowel movement, do you lose weight?\" is: No, having a bowel movement does not result in a significant loss of body weight or body fat. The weight loss associated with having a bowel movement is minimal and temporary, and it is not a reliable indicator of weight loss or fat loss. Instead, weight loss occurs through a calorie deficit, which forces the body to burn stored fat for energy.", "response": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 27, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, an ad hominem fallacy is an attack on an argument made by attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. On the other hand, poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered and redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties. In summary, both types of attacks involve attacking the person making the argument, but poisoning the well fallacy specifically takes place before the merits of a case are considered.", "response": "The ad hominem fallacy directly attacks the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy attacks the integrity or intelligence of one of the parties before the merits of the case can be considered.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 28, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "ground_truth": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "response": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, select the data, click on the Sort button, and select the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 29, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "temperature bucharest", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the current temperature in Bucharest, Romania is:\n\nPassage 1 does not provide real-time weather data, so I cannot find the current temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 2 provides a map of UK weather warnings and flood warnings, but it does not provide information on the temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 3 provides general information about the climate in Bucharest, including the average monthly weather patterns, but it does not provide the current temperature. Therefore, I am unable to answer your question based on these passages.", "response": "Bucharest has a humid continental climate. Winters can get windy and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 30, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "ground_truth": "To make panko crumbs, preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 degrees F for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.", "response": "To make panko crumbs, preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 31, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to find pictures you deleted on your messaging on iphone", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain information on how to find pictures that have been deleted from the Messages app on an iPhone. The first passage discusses deleting text message conversations, while the second and third passages focus on recovering deleted photos from an iPhone or iCloud backup. None of the passages provide instructions on how to retrieve deleted pictures from the Messages app.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 32, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "ground_truth": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first determine the extent of the tarnish. If the jewelry is slightly dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth into the solution. Rub the jewelry with the cloth, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. If the tarnish is heavier, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the jewelry and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. If your silver jewelry is lightly tarnished, you can also try submerging it in a hot saltwater bath. Ensure that if your jewelry has gemstones, they won't be affected by the saltwater. For diamonds, clean with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, and pat dry with a soft cloth.", "response": "Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water, wet the silver, and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 33, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "ground_truth": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help in the regeneration of the forest. Fires consume dead and decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Jack pines rely on fire to spread their seeds. They produce seratonous (resin-filled) cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, causing the cones to open and the seeds to fall or blow out. Furthermore, fires can disrupt the growth of other trees like spruce, providing an advantage to the more fire-tolerant jack pines and allowing them to proliferate.", "response": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they are the mechanism by which the forest is continually regenerated. Fires consume dead, decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 70.09, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 34, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of cupping massage", "ground_truth": "Cupping massage has several benefits. It is known to help eliminate toxins from the body and improve blood circulation. It also aids in pain relief by reducing tissue inflammation, which subsequently improves flexibility and increases range of motion. Additionally, cupping massage has mental benefits such as decreasing anxiety and depression.", "response": "The benefits of cupping massage include eliminating toxins, improving circulation, pain relief, and mental benefits like decreasing anxiety and depression.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 35, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the process used to extract it. Refined coconut oil is extracted from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is extracted from the flesh of the fresh coconut. Another difference is that refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point and is therefore better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no taste or smell, while unrefined oil retains its distinctive coconut flavor and aroma.", "response": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and has a higher smoking point of 450°F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. It is deodorized, meaning it has no discernible taste or smell. Unrefined coconut oil, also called pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350°F. It carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 36, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is why your Snapchat account might be temporarily locked:\n\n1. Using third-party apps to access Snapchat without authorization: According to passage 2, Snapchat does not guarantee the security of accounts accessed through third-party apps. If you have been using such apps, it could result in your account being locked.\n2. Exceeding the limit of warnings for third-party app usage: Passage 1 mentions that Snapchat sends warnings before locking accounts that use third-party apps excessively. If you have exceeded the limit of warnings, your account might be temporarily locked.\n\nTherefore, the most likely reason for your Snapchat account being temporarily locked is due to the unauthorized use of third-party apps.", "response": "Your Snapchat account may be temporarily locked due to the use of third-party apps.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 37, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "ground_truth": "Salary exchange pension contributions, also known as salary sacrifice, is a method where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This can allow both employers and employees to save money. The salary that is waived under the salary exchange is equal to the value of the regular pension contribution made. For example, it could be 7.5% or 9% of the pay, depending on the pension scheme. The employer then pays a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme.", "response": "Salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee giving up part of their salary in exchange for a pension payment, with the value of the salary waived being equal to the regular pension contribution to USS, USPAS, or SGSS.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 38, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that porterhouse steak is a larger version of T-Bone steak and it contains more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steak.", "response": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 6.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 39, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "temperature for tallahassee florida", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the average high temperature in Tallahassee, Florida is 79 degrees Fahrenheit and the average low is 56 degrees Fahrenheit.", "response": "The average high temperature in Tallahassee, Florida, is 79 degrees Fahrenheit, and the average low temperature is 56 degrees Fahrenheit.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 86.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 40, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what traits do people have that are born in october?", "ground_truth": "People born in October are described as having a keen interest in and an eye for form and structure, which can make them good architects, interior decorators, designers, or any profession that combines art and structure. They are also described as success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful individuals. They are at their best when they are in control, their own boss, or working on their own. They can also get along with others and possess necessary \"people skills\", although they can occasionally show impatience. Despite being restless at heart, they crave stability and security, which is why they work hard at whatever they do.", "response": "People born in October have a great interest in form and structure, are success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful, and are best when they are in control, their own boss, or working on their own.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 41, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to do the skill moves on fifa 16 for xbox one", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to perform skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One:\n\n1. Ball Juggle (while standing): Press and hold the LT button on the Xbox controller, followed by a quick tap of the RB button.\n\nThat's it! This combination will allow you to perform the ball juggling skill move while standing on the field in FIFA 16 on Xbox One.", "response": "To perform the Ball Juggle skill move in FIFA 16 on the Xbox One, players should hold down the LT button and tap the RB button.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 42, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "where does 1099-patr go on 1040", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"Where does 1099-PATR go on 1040?\" is:\n\nSchedule C, Schedule F, or Form 4835.\n\nAccording to the instructions for Form 1099-PATR, patronage dividends and other distributions in boxes 1, 2, 3, and 5 from a cooperative are reported on one of these forms.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 43, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "ground_truth": "To create an employee schedule, start by making a list of all employees and their duties (Passage 2). Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day (Passage 2). Print out copies of the schedule for employees or send them via email (Passage 3). If you need to make any changes, keep a master schedule and update it as needed (Passage 3). Microsoft Excel is a useful tool for creating schedules for multiple employees and can be used as your business grows (Passage 3). It's important to note that there may be other work laws that you need to follow, such as paying overtime if you schedule an employee more than 40 hours per week (Passage 1).", "response": "To create employee schedules, you can make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform, then make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 44, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "ground_truth": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay close to them when they are near the three-point line, actively sliding your feet to minimize shot opportunities (passage 1). It is important to create a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player (passage 3).", "response": "Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 45, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are the key similarities and differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system:\n\nSimilarities:\n\n* Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n* Both systems use chemical messengers (neurotransmitters and hormones) to transmit signals.\n* Both systems have negative feedback mechanisms to regulate their function.\n\nDifferences:\n\n* The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of glands.\n* Transmission of signals occurs through electrical impulses in the nervous system, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n* The nervous system has a continuous structure, with cells connected to each other, while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs not physically connected to each other.\n* The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system to transmit signals.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands. Transmission is performed by the electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, whereas hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system. The", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 46, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "ground_truth": "To plant a potato that has sprouted, first cut large potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, being careful not to break the long sprouts. Place these chunks on a tray and let them dry out in a cool, dark place overnight. Small, sprouted potatoes can be planted whole. Next, prepare your planting area by turning the soil over with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches, removing any large rocks or debris. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. Cut your potatoes into cubes of about 1 to 2 inches, making sure to leave a sprout on each cube. Place these cubes in the trench, sprouted side facing up, spaced about 6 to 8 inches apart. Cover the potatoes with compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings. Water the potatoes thoroughly and regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Finally, add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, keeping it at least 4 inches away from the sprouting potato vines. This mulch will help keep the soil cool and maintain a consistent moisture level.", "response": "Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. Small potatoes can be planted whole. Water the potatoes thoroughly. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 47, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "color of urin meaning", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine can indicate various things. Here's what we can infer from the passages:\n\n* Red urine (passage 1) indicates the presence of blood in the urine, which can be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer.\n* Deep purple urine (passage 2) is associated with porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Certain foods and medications can also change urine color.\n* The normal color of urine is pale yellow (passage 3), but this color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases where the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is the meaning of different colors of urine?\" based on these passages is:\n\nRed urine can indicate the presence of blood in the urine, while deep purple urine is associated with porphyria. Changes in urine color can also be caused by kidney diseases.", "response": "The color of urine can provide important clues about a person's health. Red urine is typically a sign of blood in the urine and can be a sign of serious conditions like infections or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Certain foods and medications can also change urine color.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.47, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 48, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "ground_truth": "When you breathe in, or inhale, the intercostal muscles contract and expand the ribcage while the diaphragm contracts and pulls downward to increase the volume of the chest. This lowers the pressure inside the chest and allows air to be sucked into the lungs through the windpipe. When you breathe out, or exhale, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, and the intercostal muscles also relax. This reduces the space in the chest cavity and forces out air that is rich in carbon dioxide out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "response": "When you breathe in (inhale), the diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. The intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. As a result, the pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out (exhale), the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, and the intercostal muscles also relax, reducing the space in the chest cavity. This causes air rich in carbon dioxide to be forced out of your lungs and windpipe.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 17}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 78.95, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 49, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "inventory costing weighted average", "ground_truth": "Sure! Here's my answer to the question:\n\nThe weighted average method of costing inventory assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. When a unit of inventory is sold, the weighted average method takes the average cost of all inventories currently available and assigns that average price to the item sold. Since inventory prices fluctuate, the weighted average cost will also change.\n\nTo calculate the weighted average cost per unit, divide the cost of goods available for sale by the number of units available for sale. The weighted-average figure can then be used to assign costs to both ending inventory and cost of goods sold. The recorded amount of inventory on hand using the weighted average costing method represents a value between the oldest and newest units purchased into stock.\n\nWeighted average costing is commonly used in situations where inventory items are intermingled and it is impossible to assign a specific cost to an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sophisticated enough to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers.", "response": "The weighted average method of costing inventory assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. When a unit of inventory is sold, the average cost of all inventories currently available is taken. This average price is then assigned to the item sold. Since inventory prices fluctuate, the weighted average cost will also change.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 50, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not directly increase your Snapchat score. The score is primarily based on the number of snaps sent and received.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 51, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "ground_truth": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. It aids in the development of gross motor skills as they engage in activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water from buckets. Water play also facilitates academic learning in areas such as science and math. Children learn about the concept of floating and sinking, and understand that different objects have different buoyancies. In math, they learn about measurement by determining the amount of water that fits into a bucket, and concepts of more and less by comparing water levels in different buckets. Water play also promotes creativity, allowing children to use their imagination.", "response": "Children learn gross motor skills, academic skills in science and math, and creativity with water play.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 52, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what exercises tone the chest", "ground_truth": "Sure! Based on the given passages, the following exercises are mentioned as toning the chest:\n\n* Modified tri-set for the chest (not specified)\n* Pushups\n* Dumbbell bench presses\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What exercises tone the chest?\" based on the given passages is:\n\nModified tri-set for the chest, pushups, and dumbbell bench presses.", "response": "pushups and very heavy sets of dumbbell bench presses", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 53, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the breathing process involves the contraction and relaxation of various muscles, including the diaphragm muscle, to move air in and out of the lungs. This process involves an exchange of gases between the body and the external environment, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity by contracting the muscles involved in breathing draws air into the lungs, causing them to expand and decreasing air pressure below atmospheric pressure. Therefore, the passage does not mention any specific step involved in processing air before it reaches the lungs.", "response": "The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 6.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nMagellan of Virginia does offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses. According to passage 1, Magellan is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB).\n\nAdditionally, Magellan of Virginia has been selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. This is mentioned in passage 2.\n\nFinally, Magellan of Virginia offers a Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for providers to address their questions and issues. This is mentioned in passage 3.", "response": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 20.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "ground_truth": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet sprayed with butter flavored cooking spray. Optionally, layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish is cooked and flakes easily. If desired, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven for approximately 3 minutes to allow the cheese to melt.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven to allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 90.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 2, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun before attempting to scrape it off. However, if the plastic cannot be removed completely, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "response": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, you can follow the steps described in the first passage. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 76.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 3, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the benefits of a water pick include maintaining good oral health, reducing the risk of gingivitis, cleaning better around the teeth and gums, and eliminating tough-to-remove germs and plaque from the gum line.", "response": "A water pick is a useful oral care tool that can help maintain good oral health. It can massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, which helps to reduce the risk of gingivitis. Water Pik also helps to clean better around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing can not access.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 4, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "set default browser to windows", "ground_truth": "Method 1 of 2 in passage 2 provides the steps to set the default web browser in Windows 7.", "response": "To set the default browser in Windows, follow the specific method provided in the second passage. Open the Settings app by clicking the Settings icon in the Start menu or using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut. In the left-pane, click Default apps. In the right-side, scroll down to see the Web browser section. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as the default browser.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 5, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook brats", "ground_truth": "Based on the passages provided, the steps to cook brats are as follows:\n\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook. \n2. Combine beer and onions in a large pot and bring it to a boil. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer, adding red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. In the meantime, preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.\n5. After simmering, remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and reduce the heat to low, continuing to cook the onions.\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally, for about 10 to 14 minutes until they are browned evenly.\n7. Serve the bratwurst with the beer and onion mixture as a topping or side.", "response": "To cook brats\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Prick bratwurst with fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n3. Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n4. Place pot over medium heat, and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Cook bratwurst on preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 6, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "ground_truth": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "response": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps: First, place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Next, take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touching the blood with one end of the slide. Allow the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action, pushing carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place in the provided slide transport containers.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 72.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 7, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "typical weather in indiana", "ground_truth": "The typical weather in Indiana is characterized by long, warm, humid, and wet summers. The winters are chilly and windy with some snowfall. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F and is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F. The state also experiences some rainfall, with the wettest year recording 57.65 inches of rain and the driest 24.97 inches. The most snowfall recorded in a season was 74.5 inches.", "response": "The typical weather in Indiana is characterized by long, warm, humid summers and chilly, windy winters. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F, with temperatures rarely dropping below 3°F or rising above 92°F.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 8, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how the body systems work together", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 7.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 9.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 9, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, water shares can be transferred through the issuance of a new Water Stock Certificate to the new owner of record after paying a fee of $75.00. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner must provide proof of ownership before a transfer can be processed. Additionally, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the company and must be signed and notarized.", "response": "The process of transferring water shares involves returning the Water Stock Certificate, paying a fee of $75.00, providing proof of ownership, and receiving a new Water Stock Certificate.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 10, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the process of building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids, cutting and assembling the floor with 2 x 6 rim joists and joists, anchoring the frame to the skids, attaching tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing the walls separately, and raising them onto the frame.", "response": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches, cutting two 2 x 6 rim joists and six joists at 7 3/4 and 44 3/4 inches respectively, and assembling the floor on the skids. The floor is checked for square and then anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and raised onto the frame. The shed shown in the passage is 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 11, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "ground_truth": "Sure! Here's how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nTo roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices, if desired.\n7. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for up to 45 minutes or until the cloves are softened to your liking.\n8. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nNote that the roasting time may vary depending on the size of your garlic cloves, so check on them periodically to avoid overcooking.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers. Use a sharp knife to cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 12, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sew a zipper gusset:\n\n1. Make a casing in the side seams by stitching the outer edge of the gusset and the back side seam.\n2. Slide the boning right down into the casing.\n3. Push the seam allowance to the back and tack the casing to the lining, if necessary, so it doesn't move.\n4. Make a zipper sandwich by placing one piece of lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down.\n5. Sew across the top of the zipper sandwich with a zipper foot, making sure to line up the three edges.\n6. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper.\n7. Trace all pattern pieces to the remaining fabric and cut them out.\n8. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, with the right sides facing each other, and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n9. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the zipper gusset, with the right sides facing down, and stitch along the seam line.\n10. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n11. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\n12. The width of the zipper between the gusset should measure 1/2\".\n13. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch along the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabrics together nicely.\n\nTherefore, to sew a zipper gusset, you need to make a casing in the side seams, insert the boning, make a zipper sandwich, sew the zipper gusset to the zipper, and attach the lining to the zipper gusset.", "response": "To sew a zipper gusset, first make a zipper sandwich by placing the lining fabric face up, then the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down. Line up the three edges and sew across the top between the edge of your zipper sandwich and the zipper teeth. Then, pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 65.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 13, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to soften sugar", "ground_truth": "To soften brown sugar, you can place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Then put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. To make hardened granulated sugar soft again, preheat an oven to its lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its package and put it in an ovenproof container. Place it in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "response": "Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.6, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 14, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "ground_truth": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 375°F or 450°F. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Rub the roast with seasoning, and season it with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Roast for 1 hour or 15 minutes, respectively, and then turn off the oven", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.96, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 15, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "ground_truth": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused primarily by bacteria, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci, also known as Streptococcus pyogenes. This is the same bacteria that causes strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria types, such as staphylococcus, are also associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. Prior trauma, such as a cut or scrape, insect bite, burn, or needle puncture wound can serve as a source of infection as well as surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures. In rare cases, fungi can lead to this condition.", "response": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS) and staphylococcus. These bacteria can cause infections such as strep throat and impetigo. While the infections caused by these bacteria are usually mild, they can sometimes lead to a more dangerous infection, such as", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 16, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "ground_truth": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, with all atoms having the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded, allowing for easy separation of the components using physical methods.", "response": "Elements are composed of only one type of atom, compounds are composed of two or more different elements and are chemically bonded, and mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 17, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "ground_truth": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "response": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 18, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do crab traps work", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, a crab trap is a large square metal cage with a system of nets inside that allows crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the top. To set the trap, the ends with lead-ins are placed in the water and the crabs are attracted to the free meal offered by the trap. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game recommends using king crab pots that range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights between 2 and 3 feet. Over time, these mechanisms may disable the trap, preventing it from ghost fishing.", "response": "Crab traps work by using a large metal cage with wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The crab pot has an entrance (a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot) and two lead-ins (angles into the trap from the sides and bottom) that crabs must crawl up to reach their meal.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 19, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "ground_truth": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side or until they are no longer pink inside.", "response": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 5.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 75.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 20, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "the benefits of msm powder", "ground_truth": "The benefits of MSM powder include helping to get oxygen into the blood more efficiently, increasing energy levels by making cell walls more permeable, aiding in the absorption of nutrients, relieving muscular aches and pains, and reducing inflammation due to injury or inflammatory diseases such as arthritis.", "response": "Increased oxygen efficiency", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 21, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a condition where there is significant bone density loss, leading to symptoms such as sudden and severe back pain, loss of height, and an increased risk of fractures, particularly in the spine, hips, and wrists.", "response": "Severe osteoporosis may involve sudden, severe back pain, loss of height over time, fractures of vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 22, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "ground_truth": "To properly fertilize your grass, you should fertilize at the beginning of the growing season for your specific grass type. For warm season grasses, this would be when the grass turns green in the early spring. You should also know the type of fertilizer to use based on the type of grass you have and do a pH soil test to ensure the fertilizer has the appropriate pH for your soil. Once you've determined the correct fertilizer and timing, apply it in a perpendicular pattern and check the lawn after application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape, but if it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "response": "proper way to fertilize your grass involves fertilizing at the right time of year, knowing your grass type, doing a pH soil test, measuring your lawn, applying the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, and checking the turf's response to ensure the lawn is in good shape.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 23, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's how to make a hot water heater circulate:\n\nOption 1: Install a recirculating pump. Passage 3 explains that recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These pumps can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.\n\nOption 2: Use a hot water circulation pump. Passage 2 describes how a hot water circulation pump can send cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, ensuring that hot water is always available when needed.\n\nIt is important to note that running a hot water circulation pump continuously can consume a significant amount of energy, as mentioned in passage 1. Therefore, it may be more cost-effective to only run the pump when needed, such as when you turn on the faucet.", "response": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This pump circulates water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 24, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how well do patterned rollers work", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here's what we can conclude about how well patterned rollers work:\n\nPassage 1 suggests that homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than commercial ones for certain faux finishes because they can create a random pattern of texture.\n\nPassage 2 provides a personal testimonial about the effectiveness of the Dermaroller for improving the appearance of skin. The writer claims that it makes their skin look younger and healthier, and that it works best when used with serums or moisturizers. However, there is no direct mention of patterned rollers in this passage.\n\nPassage 3 provides instructions for creating a basic texture roller using an old roller pad with clumped tufts and random patterns created by stretching and twisting rubber bands. This passage suggests that patterned rollers can create a textured finish on walls, but there is no information on how effective they are or how well they work.\n\nTherefore, based on the given passages, it is difficult to say definitively how well patterned rollers work. Passage 1 suggests that they may be effective for certain applications, while passage 2 provides a personal endorsement of a specific product (Dermaroller) for improving skin appearance. Passage 3 provides instructions for creating a basic texture roller, but does not provide any information on its effectiveness. Therefore, the answer to the original question is: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "Patterned rollers work well for applying a random pattern of texture to walls, which is crucial for certain faux finishes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.72, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 25, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make ribs", "ground_truth": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "response": "To make ribs, you can grill them or oven-cook them. To grill ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F), remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes. To oven-cook ribs, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs, put the ribs in a resealable bag, add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover, and line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 71.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 26, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what political, economic and social effects have on the united states", "ground_truth": "The passages provided offer some insights into the political, economic, and social effects of various events in the history of the United States.\n\nPassage 1 highlights the impact of immigration on the country, indicating that it has shaped the nation since its early days. Immigration has contributed to the diversity of the population, cultural exchange, and the development of the economy.\n\nPassage 2 discusses the long-term effects of Reconstruction, which include the continuation of racial discrimination, segregation, and unequal access to employment opportunities for African Americans. This period saw the introduction of crop lien work contracts, which kept many African Americans in a state of virtual slavery.\n\nPassage 3 discusses the economic and political effects of the Civil War. The war brought economic unity to the country, as the South transitioned from a semi-subsistence economy to a market-based economy, and industrialization gained momentum. The passage also notes that important political changes accompanied the maintenance of national unity.\n\nBased on these passages, we can infer that the political, economic, and social effects of these historical events in the United States include:\n\n1. Immigration: Shaping the nation's population, culture, and economy.\n2. Reconstruction: Continued racial discrimination, segregation, and unequal access to employment opportunities for African Americans.\n3. Civil War: Economic unity, industrialization, and political changes that maintained national unity.\n\nTherefore, the political, economic, and social effects of these events in the United States include increased diversity, economic growth, and the continued struggle for racial equality.", "response": "The political, economic, and social effects of Reconstruction on the United States included the maintenance of national unity, the arrival of industrialization and large economic enterprises, and the challenges faced by African Americans in finding work and being hired.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 27, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is the difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy:\n\nAd hominem fallacy refers to attacking an argument by attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. Poisoning the well fallacy, on the other hand, is a specific type of ad hominem attack that occurs before the merits of a case can be considered, and it redirects the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.\n\nIn other words, ad hominem fallacy is a broader term that encompasses various types of attacks on the person making the argument, while poisoning the well fallacy is a specific type of ad hominem attack that focuses on the person's integrity or intelligence.", "response": "The ad hominem fallacy attacks the person directly, while the poisoning the well fallacy attacks the person indirectly before the discussion of the merits of the argument.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 28, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "ground_truth": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "response": "Select the Data tab, click on the Sort button, and select Custom Sort from the popup menu. Then, select the data to sort by (in this example, the Product column) and click on the OK button.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 29, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "temperature bucharest", "ground_truth": "Based on passage 3, the average temperature in Bucharest, Romania during July and August is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures can also reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "response": "Bucharest has a humid continental climate. Winters can get windy and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °Fahrenheit), sometimes even dropping to minus 20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 30, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\nPassage 1 states to push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 2 provides similar instructions, stating to push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional information, suggesting to preheat the oven to 300°F before making the crumbs. The passage also recommends using a blender carafe to pulse the bread until coarse crumbs form, and then spreading the crumbs evenly on two half-sheet pans and baking until they just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. After cooling the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, transfer them to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nTherefore, to make panko crumbs based on the provided passages, you can use a food processor or blender to shred or pulse bread into coarse crumbs, and then bake them in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.59, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 31, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is a upc description", "ground_truth": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, a barcode symbology used extensively in multiple countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and in Europe. It is used for tracking trade items in stores. UPC consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is primarily used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "response": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, uniquely assigned to each trade item.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 32, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "ground_truth": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use a few different methods based on the passages provided. For silver jewelry, you can mix mild dish soap with warm water, dip a soft cloth into the mixture, and rub the jewelry. Then rinse it in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry. If the tarnish is heavier, you can make a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water, apply it to the silver with a soft cloth, and rinse it off. For diamonds, you can clean them with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, then pat them dry with a soft cloth. If you have silver jewelry with gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.", "response": "Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth (not paper towels, which can scratch).", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.91, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 33, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways:\n\n1. Fire helps to clear the way for new growth by consuming dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, creating a clean slate for seed germination and seedling establishment (Passage 2).\n2. Jack pine seeds are adapted to fire, as they are stored in serotinous cones that only open after a fire has melted the resin holding them closed. This allows the seeds to disperse and establish new populations (Passage 2).\n3. Fire can create a favorable environment for jack pine and aspen regrowth by reducing competition from other tree species, such as spruce, which have better access to sunlight while shading the other trees (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, forest fires can benefit jack pines by providing a means of seed dispersal and creating conditions that promote their growth and regeneration.", "response": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they serve as a mechanism for forest regeneration, clearing the way for new growth. The jack pine, in particular, relies on fire for seed dispersal, as the cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, causing the cones to pop open and release the seeds.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.39, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 34, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of cupping massage", "ground_truth": "Cupping massage has several benefits including eliminating toxins from the body, improved circulation, pain relief, and mental benefits such as reducing anxiety and depression.", "response": "The benefits of cupping massage include eliminating toxins, improving circulation, providing pain relief, and offering mental benefits such as decreasing anxiety and depression.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 35, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "response": "Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit and has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F). Unrefined coconut oil, also called pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of the fresh coconuts and has a distinct aroma and flavor. Refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature coconut flavor and has no discernible taste or smell.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 36, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "why is my snapchat temporarily locked", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, it appears that your Snapchat account has been temporarily locked due to using third-party apps. According to passage 2, Snapchat does not guarantee security when using third-party apps, and they may lock your account if they detect such usage. Passage 3 also mentions that Snapchat has taken steps to punish individuals who use third-party apps, which could result in account lockout.\n\nIt's possible that you have been warned multiple times by Snapchat about using third-party apps, as mentioned in passage 1, and your account has been locked as a result. To regain access to your account, you may need to stop using third-party apps and wait for an official Snapchat app to become available for your device, as suggested in passage 2.", "response": "Your Snapchat account is temporarily locked because you used a third-party application to access Snapchat.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.82, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 37, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "ground_truth": "Salary exchange pension contributions allow employees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement benefits both employers and employees as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary, and employees can save money by making pension contributions through this method. The amount of salary waived under the salary exchange is equivalent to the regular pension contribution, and the employer pays a corresponding amount into the pension scheme. The specific details of the contributions may vary depending on the pension scheme being used.", "response": "Salary exchange is a pension contribution method where an employee gives up part of their salary in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer, leading to lower NICs for the employer.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.45, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 38, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it appears that the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their location within the sirloin muscle. Sirloin steaks are cut from the back of the animal and continue off the short loin from which other cuts such as T-bone and porterhouse steaks are made. On the other hand, porterhouse steaks are specifically carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin and therefore have more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to T-bone steaks. However, the passages suggest that both sirloin and porterhouse steaks may be referred to as the same thing or as a large version of the T-bone due to their similarity in appearance and taste.", "response": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 39, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "temperature for tallahassee florida", "ground_truth": "The average temperature for Tallahassee, Florida is 79 degrees Fahrenheit (26 degrees Celsius) high and 56 degrees Fahrenheit (13 degrees Celsius) low.", "response": "Tallahassee, Florida has an overall average high temperature of 79 degrees and an average low of 56 degrees.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 40, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what traits do people have that are born in october?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are some traits associated with people born in October:\n\n* Interest in form and structure (Passage 1)\n* Success-oriented and charming (Passage 2)\n* Personal power and impatience (Passage 2)\n* Crave stability and security (Passage 3)\n\nHowever, it's important to note that these are generalizations based on astrological signs and not all individuals will exhibit these traits. Additionally, there is no information about specific personality traits or characteristics of people born in October. Therefore, I cannot provide a more detailed answer based solely on the given passages.", "response": "People born in October have a variety of traits, including an interest in form and structure", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 41, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to do the skill moves on fifa 16 for xbox one", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's how to do skill moves on FIFA 16 for Xbox One:\n\n1. Ball Juggle (while standing): Hold LT + tap RB.\n\nNote that this combination works for Xbox 360 and Xbox One controllers. If you're playing on PC with a controller, the buttons may be different. Additionally, there are tutorial videos available online that show what each skill move looks like, which can be helpful in mastering these moves.", "response": "To perform the Ball Juggle skill move on FIFA 16 for Xbox One, hold the LT button and tap the RB button.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 42, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "where is dove soap headquarters", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the headquarters of Dove Soap can be located in:\n\nPassage 1 states that if you want to speak to a live representative, you can call them at 1-800-761-DOVE (3683) from Monday to Friday between 8:30 AM to 6:00 PM Eastern Time. This suggests that the headquarters of Dove Soap is located in the Eastern Time zone.\n\nPassage 2 provides the same phone number as Passage 1 for contacting a live representative, but also notes that this number is available 24 hours a day / 7 days a week for medical or product safety emergencies. This indicates that the headquarters of Dove Soap is open for business operations 24/7.\n\nPassage 3 does not provide any information about the location of Dove Soap's headquarters.\n\nTherefore, based on the given passages, the headquarters of Dove Soap can be located in the Eastern Time zone and is open for business operations 24/7.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 43, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to create an employee schedule:\n\n1. Talk to a lawyer about work laws: It is important to understand the legal requirements for creating an employee schedule, including paying overtime for hours worked beyond 40 per week. Additionally, there may be other laws to consider, such as restrictions for employees under the age of 18.\n2. Use scheduling software or a simple word processing program: You can create an employee schedule using scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or even a sheet of paper. Make a list of all employees and their duties, and create a chart of work days and hours for each day.\n3. Print or send schedules to employees: Once you have created the schedule, print out copies for each employee or send them to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule for making any changes. If you are using a digital tool, you can easily edit and share the schedule with employees.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to create an employee schedule, such as setting up the schedule format, determining pay rates, or communicating the schedule to employees.", "response": "To create employee schedules, you can use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day, and print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 44, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "ground_truth": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you can stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, you can keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player and defend against them with tips from an experienced basketball player.", "response": "Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.79, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 45, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "ground_truth": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here are the key differences and similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system:\n\nDifferences:\n\n* The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n* Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while in the endocrine system, it is done through chemicals called hormones.\n* The nervous system is continuous and interconnected, while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs.\n* The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system.\n\nSimilarities:\n\n* Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n* Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n* Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs.\n\nTherefore, based on the given passages, the nervous system and endocrine system have different structures and methods of transmission, but they share similar functions and regulatory mechanisms.", "response": "The nervous system and the endocrine system are both involved in maintaining homeostasis and are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Chemical messengers play a significant role in both systems. However, they differ in the following ways: the nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands; transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas hormones in the endocrine system transmit signals; the nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected; the nervous system uses neurons for signal transmission, while the endocrine system utilizes the circulatory system.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 46, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "ground_truth": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and let them dry out overnight. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in a prepared planting area. Place the sprouted or eye side of the potato chunks facing up, separating each chunk by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants to keep the soil cool and maintain moisture.", "response": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each, place the chunks on a tray or cookie sheet to dry out overnight, and then plant the cut chunks in a trench with the sprouted side", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 47, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "ground_truth": "To properly clean your hair, first select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. Ensure your water is warm but not too hot, and thoroughly wet your hair. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through the hair. If your hair is long, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles rather than piling it on your head. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove any tangles. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and let it stay on for a few minutes. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Pat dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoid rubbing it with the towel as it can cause damage. For complete drying, a hair dryer can be used.", "response": "To properly clean your hair, follow these steps: First, select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. Ensure the water is warm but not too hot and turn down the flow slightly. Thoroughly wet the hair, then apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo and work it through the hair with your fingers. Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this will cause damage to the hair.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 6.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 48, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "ground_truth": "When you breathe in, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm also contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. This lowers the pressure inside the chest, allowing air to be sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward, and the intercostal muscles also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. This forces air rich in carbon dioxide out of the lungs and windpipe, and then out of the nose or mouth.", "response": "When you breathe in, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage, and the diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered, causing air to be sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, and the intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of the lungs and windpipe, and then out of the nose or mouth.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 85.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 49, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "inventory costing weighted average", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to your question:\n\nThe weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. The cost of goods available for sale is divided by the number of units available for sale to calculate the weighted-average cost per unit. This figure is then used to assign a cost to both ending inventory and the cost of goods sold. The weighted average method is commonly used when inventory items are intermingled and cannot be assigned a specific cost, or when the accounting system is not sophisticated enough to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers.", "response": "assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 50, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "ground_truth": "No, based on the given passages, it does not seem like watching Snapchat stories directly increases one's score. However, sending and receiving more snaps, including opening all received snaps, can help increase the score.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 51, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "ground_truth": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers and pouring water. Water play also provides opportunities for academic learning, such as understanding concepts like floating and sinking, measuring water, and comparing quantities. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children pretend and engage in imaginative play with water.", "response": "children learn gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 52, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "ground_truth": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, first, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod, then crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it remains upright and no water gets inside. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for about six minutes. After cooking, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Finally, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate. The PoachPod can be cleaned in a dishwasher.", "response": "Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 53, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the process of processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs involves the following steps:\n\n1. The diaphragm muscle contracts to take air into the lungs, moving down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region. (Passage 1)\n2. The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment, occurring in the lungs. (Passage 2)\n3. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity, including the lungs, decreases the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing us to inhale. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the main steps in processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs are:\n\n1. Contraction of the diaphragm muscle to draw air into the lungs.\n2. Exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment in the lungs.\n3. Expansion of the thoracic cavity to decrease air pressure in the lungs and facilitate inhalation.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "response": "The process of air before it gets to your lungs involves the exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment, which is the air.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "ground_truth": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not mention anything about Magellan of Virginia's status as a provider or its relationship with other providers. Passage 1 discusses Magellan's ability to offer continuing education credits, while Passage 2 explains its role as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Passage 3 mentions a weekly call for providers to ask questions and address issues, but it does not provide information about Magellan's status as a provider. Therefore, I cannot answer the question based on the given passages.", "response": "Magellan of Virginia provides continuing education clock hours/credits, is approved by the APA and ASWB, is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs, and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "ground_truth": "To cook pollock, first, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Then, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Next, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily. If desired, you can also add cheese on top of the pollock fillets and bake for an additional 3 minutes to melt the cheese.", "response": "Bake pollock fillets in a preheated oven at 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) for about 15 minutes until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 2, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic does not come off with this method, another option is to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic until it becomes soft and pliable. Then, attempt to peel it off carefully. However, be aware that this method may not work, and in that case, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. It is recommended to call a service technician for this type of repair.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to get plastic out of clothes dryer is:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper.\n3. Apply nail polish remover to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Rinse with a damp cloth and soap solution.\n5. Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic if necessary.\n\nIf the plastic still does not come off, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer.", "response": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, you can use a plastic scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution. Rub the area again with the cloth. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. If the plastic is difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. You may not be able to get all of the plastic off. If not, you need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, I recommend calling a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 3, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, the benefits of using a water pick (also known as a Waterpik) include:\n\n1. Helping to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier by eliminating germs and plaque.\n2. Being a great oral care tool for removing food from areas that brushing cannot access.\n3. Massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth to reduce the risk of gingivitis.\n4. Being an alternative to flossing and potentially offering similar benefits.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on other potential benefits of using a water pick, such as its ability to reach areas between teeth or its effectiveness in reducing plaque buildup.", "response": "A water pick helps to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier, eliminates pesky germs and plaque that are tough to get rid of with a toothbrush, can massage and stimulate soft tissue in the mouth, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and helps to clean better around the teeth and gums, removing food from areas that brushing can not access.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 4, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "set default browser to windows", "ground_truth": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "response": "To set the default browser to Windows, follow these steps:", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 5.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 5, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook brats", "ground_truth": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n4. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and continue cooking on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "response": "To cook brats, you should first preheat the grill to medium-high heat. Then, prick the brats with a fork to prevent them from exploding while cooking. Place the brats in a large stock pot with onions, brown the onions in the butter for 1-2 minutes, stirring them frequently to ensure they are browned on all sides. Brown the brats on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 6, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "ground_truth": "Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here are the steps to prepare a blood slide based on the provided passages:\n\n1. First, sterilize a needle with a flame as described in Passage 1.\n2. Next, obtain a blood sample by pricking your finger or using a blood donation kit. This will require adult supervision, especially if you are doing it yourself.\n3. Place a drop of blood towards one end of a clean glass slide as instructed in Passage 2.\n4. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide through capillary action. Gently push the blood along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Repeat this step to make two smears.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely before labeling them clearly and placing them in the provided slide transport containers as suggested in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "response": "Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface, add one small drop of blood to one end, take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide to produce a thin smear, make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, label them clearly, and place them in provided slide transport containers.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 7, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "typical weather in indiana", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the typical weather in Indiana includes long, warm, humid, and wet summers, and chilly and windy winters. The temperature ranges from 22°F to 85°F throughout the year. The passages also mention snowfall and snow accumulation in specific cities, but do not provide a comprehensive overview of the typical weather in Indiana. Therefore, it is not possible to provide a complete answer based solely on the given passages.", "response": "The typical weather in Indiana is long, warm, humid, and wet in the summer, and chilly and windy in the winter. The temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F and is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 13}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 8, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "ground_truth": "The Windward and Leeward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea. The Windward Islands are in the southeast and are exposed to the northeast trade winds, hence they receive more rain and are wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are located in the northwest and are away from the wind, making them drier.", "response": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and are wetter, while the leeward islands are away from the wind and are drier but still receive some rain.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 9, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here's how water shares are transferred:\n\n1. Passage 1 states that a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. The passage also mentions that a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n2. Passage 2 outlines the steps required to transfer a Water Stock Certificate: (a) The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate, (b) the new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership, (c) a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and (d) a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner.\n3. Passage 3 provides general information about buying a home with water shares or rights, including the need to understand the steps involved in transferring water rights into the buyer's name. However, this passage does not provide specific instructions for transferring water shares.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the answer to the question is:\n\nTransferring water shares involves paying a fee of $75.00 to process the transfer, returning the Water Stock Certificate to the company, providing proof of ownership, and obtaining a new Water Stock Certificate in the new owner's name.", "response": "A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. The new owner of record will receive a new Water Stock Certificate. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 10, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "ground_truth": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "response": "To build a lean-to shed, start by preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length\nof 70 2/4″ and set and level them following the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 ” and six joists at\n44 3/4″. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean to shed plans. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 11, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "ground_truth": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes to an hour, or until the cloves are softened.\n7. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nYou can also season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices before roasting.", "response": "Roast individual garlic cloves by preheating the oven to 400°F (205°C), peeling and cutting the garlic, and drizzling olive oil over the exposed cloves.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 12, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to bake hard boiled egg", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how to bake hard-boiled eggs:\n\n1. Place cold eggs in a single layer in a pan with enough cold water to cover them by about 1 inch.\n2. Place the pan on the stove over high heat.\n3. As soon as the water comes to a boil, turn the heat off, cover the pan, and remove it from the heat.\n4. Allow the eggs to sit in the water for the appropriate amount of time, depending on the size of the eggs (9 minutes for medium, 12 minutes for large, and 15 minutes for extra-large).\n\nNote: Do not peek during the cooking process, and do not worry if the eggs are not perfectly symmetrical or have a slightly greenish-gray yolk.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 18}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 13, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to soften sugar", "ground_truth": "To soften sugar, place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days. Alternatively, preheat oven to lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and remove sugar from package. Put in an ovenproof container and place in the warm oven for 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "response": "To soften sugar, you can heat it in the oven at a low temperature for 15 minutes, then tap it with a spoon to help it soften. If it starts to fall apart, leave it in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 14, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "ground_truth": "To make chicken tender in a crock pot, you can cook it on low for 6 - 8 hours or until done. Alternatively, you can cook it on high for 1 hour, then on low for about 5 hours or until done. Another option is cooking it for 4 hours on high.", "response": "6 - 8 hours", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 15, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the main cause of necrotizing fasciitis is bacterial infection, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus. Additionally, other types of bacteria have also been associated with the disease. Trauma, such as cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle puncture wounds, can also play a role in the development of necrotizing fasciitis. Surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures can also serve as a source of infection. Therefore, the answer is: Bacterial infection, including group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus, and trauma.", "response": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by bacteria, with group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) being the main cause. Other types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus, can also lead to the condition.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 16, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "ground_truth": "Here are my answers to the question based on the provided passages:\n\nQ: What are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures?\nA: Based on the passages provided, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\nElements:\n\n* Are the purest form of a chemical substance (Passage 3)\n* Consist of only one type of atom with the same number of protons (Passage 3)\n\nCompounds:\n\n* Are substances composed of two or more different elements (Passage 3)\n* Are also pure substances (Passage 3)\n\nMixtures:\n\n* Contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate (Passage 1)\n* Have a variable composition (Passage 2)\n* Show the properties of their constituent substances (Passage 2)\n* Can be separated by physical means (Passage 2)", "response": "Elements are composed of only one type of atom, compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are pure substances, and mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Elements and compounds can be separated by physical means, while mixtures have a variable composition and show the properties of constituent substances and can be separated easily by physical methods.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.62, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 17, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet before starting the repair (Passage 1).\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms, and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (Passage 1).\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If necessary, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links (Passage 2).\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm (Passage 3). Secure it using pliers to ensure it is tightly fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test the toilet's flush function. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide instructions on how to fix a specific issue with the lift valve, such as a stuck or leaking valve.", "response": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, you need to follow the steps outlined in the provided passages. First, shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Next, open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 18, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do crab traps work", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are made of a metal cage with a system of nets inside, which are designed to allow crabs to enter but not escape. The traps have two leads that angle into the pot from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit entrance. The crabs crawl up the leads to reach the bait inside the pot, but cannot exit through the slit. The pot is designed to keep the crabs inside until they can be retrieved by the fisherman.\n\nAdditionally, according to passage 3, crab pots can be equipped with mechanisms that disable them over time, preventing them from continuing to catch crabs after they have been abandoned or become lost. These mechanisms can include biodegradable mesh or dissolvable cords.", "response": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 3}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.12, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 19, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "ground_truth": "To grill pork chops according to the instructions provided in Allrecipes.com, follow these steps: \n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat. \n2. Lightly oil the grate. \n3. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until well combined. \n4. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle them with the spice mixture on both sides. \n5. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. \n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side, or until they are no longer pink inside.", "response": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 76.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 20, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "the benefits of msm powder", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are the benefits of MSM powder:\n\n1. Increases energy levels by making cell walls more permeable and allowing nutrients to be absorbed more efficiently.\n2. Helps reduce inflammation and swelling in muscles and joints.\n3. Relieves muscular aches and pains.\n4. Enhances the absorption of vitamins and minerals, including Co-enzyme Q10.\n\nNote that the passages do not mention any other specific benefits of MSM powder beyond these points.", "response": "MSM powder benefits the body by increasing energy, enhancing nutrient absorption, relieving muscular aches and pains, reducing inflammation, and improving oxygen efficiency in the blood.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 21, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a advanced stage of the disease where the bones have weakened significantly, leading to severe bone loss and increased risk of fractures. At this stage, symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures are more pronounced and frequent. The risk of fractures is particularly high in the spine, hips, and wrists, and can occur even without a fall or injury.\n\nIn summary, severe osteoporosis is characterized by significant bone weakening, heightened risk of fractures, and more pronounced symptoms.", "response": "Severe osteoporosis is characterized by advanced bone density loss, increased risk of fractures, and symptoms that may include back pain, loss of height, and fractures.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 22, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to:\n\n1. Fertilize at the right time of year, which is at the beginning of the growing season, and varies for different types of grasses.\n2. Choose a fertilizer that is suitable for your type of grass and soil pH, as determined by a soil test.\n3. Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, avoiding over-fertilization, which can be determined by checking if the leaf blades bounce back up after being stepped on.", "response": "The proper way to fertilize your grass is to time the fertilization at the right time of year, conduct a pH soil test to determine the appropriate fertilizer type and frequency, measure the lawn to understand its size, apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, and check the turf's response to ensure it's in good shape.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 23, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"how to make hot water heater circulate\":\n\nA hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate water through the hot water heater and ensure that hot water is always available. The pump sends cooled water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line and circulates it through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to activate the pump and circulate the water.", "response": "A hot water circulation pump sends cool water back to the water heater through a return line, ensuring hot water availability.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 24, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how well do patterned rollers work", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it appears that patterned rollers can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, as they can produce a random pattern of texture that is often desired in faux finishing techniques. The third passage provides instructions for creating a DIY texture roller by modifying an existing roller pad with rubber bands to create clumps and random patterns, which can be used to apply paint and create a textured finish.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How well do patterned rollers work?\" is:\n\nThey can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, especially when used with faux finishing techniques.", "response": "Patterned rollers can work well, but they may not work as well on certain areas of the skin.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 25, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make ribs", "ground_truth": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Then, brush both sides of the ribs with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it sticks to the meat. Next, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up. Brush the ribs with sauce, cover the grill, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip the ribs, brush with more sauce, and cook for another 5 minutes. Repeat this process, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "response": "To make ribs, first preheat a gas or charcoal grill to medium heat (350°F to 450°F). Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.19, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 26, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "ground_truth": "Company goodwill is a business asset that is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to customer trust. This trust results in repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth, which can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients. Goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it can attract investors and future buyers, and it is an advantage of the reputation and connection with customers which tends to make that connection permanent.", "response": "Company goodwill is the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it enhances customer retention, builds trust, and attracts future buyers and investors.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 27, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "ground_truth": "The main difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is the timing of the attack. Ad hominem fallacy attacks the person making the argument instead of attacking the argument directly, but poisoning the well fallacy is a preemptive attack on a person's character or integrity before they have even made their argument. In other words, ad hominem fallacy is a reaction to an argument, while poisoning the well fallacy is a preemptive strike to discredit an opponent before they have a chance to present their argument.", "response": "The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. The poisoning the well fallacy redirects a discussion by attacking the integrity or intelligence of one of the parties before the merits of the case can be considered.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 28, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "ground_truth": "To arrange an excel sheet alphabetical, one can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n5. The data should now be sorted in alphabetical order.", "response": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, select the data you wish to sort by, then click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 76.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 29, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "ground_truth": "To remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, first remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. Additionally, there's a pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place which needs to be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off. Ensure to remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame. Finally, remove any wiring connections and the panel will come off the frame.", "response": "To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy Impala, you will\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle.\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 12}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.52, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 30, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Torn pieces of bread are pushed through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n3. The crumbs are spread on a baking sheet.\n4. The sheet is baked in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. The sheet is shaken twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. After baking, the crumbs are removed from the oven and allowed to cool completely.\n\nAlternatively, according to passage 2, you can also make panko crumbs by:\n\n1. Pushing chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n2. Spreading the crumbs on a baking sheet and baking at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n3. Shaking the sheet twice during baking.\n4. Being careful not to let the crumbs brown.\n\nFinally, passage 3 provides a third method for making panko crumbs, which involves blending the ingredients in a blender carafe and baking them on half sheet pans until they are crisp and lightly browned.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Recipe courtesy of Alton Brown, 2011.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 8}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 31, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what is a upc description", "ground_truth": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, which is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item and is mainly used for scanning items at the point of sale.", "response": "A UPC is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in various countries, consisting of 12 numeric digits, each assigned uniquely to a trade item. It is primarily used for scanning at points of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 32, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\n\n1. Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth to shine silver jewelry that is merely dull or starting to discolor. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n2. Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds. Pat the jewelry dry with a soft cloth.\n3. Soak tarnished silver jewelry in a saltwater solution of two cups of hot water. This method is gentle and can remove tarnish without abrading the silver. Make sure the gemstones will not be affected by the solution before submerging them.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to clean other types of jewelry, such as gold or platinum, or what to do if the tarnish is heavy or if the jewelry has intricate designs that may be damaged during cleaning.", "response": "Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip the jewelry in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 33, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it appears that forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help to clear away dead vegetation and promote new growth. According to passage 2, the jack pine produces serotonous cones that are dormant until a fire occurs, at which point they melt and release their seeds. This suggests that fire is a mechanism for the dispersal of jack pine seeds, and that the tree relies on fires to spread its seeds. Additionally, passage 3 suggests that while spruce trees may outcompete jack pine and aspen in some areas, fires can disrupt this cycle and allow jack pine and aspen to regain an advantage. Therefore, it seems that fires play a role in promoting the growth and survival of jack pine and other pioneer species in the boreal forest.", "response": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they are the mechanism by which the forest is continually regenerated. Some species, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine's seratonous cones are very durable and remain dormant until a fire occurs, which melts the resin and causes the cones to pop open, releasing the seeds.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 4}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 34, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits of cupping massage", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the benefits of cupping massage include eliminating toxins from the body, improving circulation, providing pain relief, increasing range of motion and flexibility, controlling pain, and decreasing anxiety and depression.", "response": "The benefits of cupping massage include eliminating toxins, improving circulation, providing pain relief, and offering mental benefits such as decreasing anxiety and depression.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 35, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "ground_truth": "Passage 3 provides information on how to change your address with the U.S. Postal Service. You can visit their website, call the USPS Call Center, or fill out and submit a form at a U.S. Post Office.", "response": "The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure change of address service that can be completed in as little as 1 minute. You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service, and the latest encryption technologies ensure your data is safe. The service can be completed online, and you can safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to your credit or debit card. You can also call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777) or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office and submitted at the Post Office.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 36, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to plan a trip to germany", "ground_truth": "To plan a trip to Germany, it is important to plan ahead and be aware of the rules and regulations regarding travel with pets. It is also recommended to research the best ways to save money during your trip, such as looking into discounted flights, cheap hotels and hostels, and affordable dining options. Additionally, learning about German life and culture can enhance your overall trip experience.", "response": "Plan a trip to Germany by considering budget travel tips, such as discounts, bargain flights, cheap hotels and hostels, restaurants, public transportation, and sightseeing. Also, consider visa requirements, when and where to go, what to see in Germany, and getting around. If traveling with pets, consider air travel with pets, vaccinations for pets, pet-friendly hotels, and rules for pets on German trains.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 37, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it appears that salary exchange is a way for employees to give up part of their salary in exchange for a pension contribution made by their employer. The salary that is waived is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution, minus any additional contributions. The employer then pays the corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to potentially save money through reduced national insurance contributions.", "response": "Salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary in exchange for a pension payment", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 38, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "history of the word gemini", "ground_truth": "Sure! Here's a brief history of the word Gemini based on the given passages:\n\nThe word \"Gemini\" comes from Latin, meaning \"twins.\" The constellation Gemini was first mentioned in Aristotle's Meteorologica over 300 years BC. In Greek mythology, the twins represented in Gemini are Castor and Pollux, who share the same mother, Leda, but have different fathers. The constellation Gemini is not in the same position as the constellation of Gemini and is a mutable sign that announces change and rules the time of year when Taurus spring has ended.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you need further clarification or if there's anything else I can help you with.", "response": "The word \"Gemini\" is a Latin word for twins and it is one of the constellations that actually look like its name would suggest. The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.49, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 39, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "ground_truth": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "response": "E-ZPass charges work by first establishing a balance on your credit card, which is $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag. As you pass through toll lanes, the system deducts the tolls from your balance until it falls below a certain value ($10 for the TX-Tag). If the balance goes below this value, the system charges your credit card another $100 or $25 to increase your balance.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": false, "fallback_source": "none", "veto_total_penalty": 0.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 0}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 40, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what traits do people have that are born in october?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here are some traits associated with people born in October:\n\n* A keen eye for form and structure (October 14)\n* Success-oriented, charming, and personally powerful (October 1)\n* Restless at heart but craving stability and security (October 5)\n\nIt's important to note that these are generalizations and not necessarily applicable to every individual born in October.", "response": "interest in structure, success, charm, personal power, and a desire for stability.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 7}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 41, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "ground_truth": "To quickly get rid of mice, you need to take immediate action. You can start by identifying all possible entry points that mice use to get into your house. Once identified, consider putting steel wool inside these holes or vents before sealing them off. This will prevent the mice from using these paths to re-enter your home. By doing so, you eliminate their access to food or shelter in your house, which can help in getting rid of them quickly.", "response": "The best way to quickly get rid of mice is to seal off entry points with steel wool.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 42, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "where is dove soap headquarters", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, I am unable to determine the location of Dove soap's headquarters. The passages only provide contact information and a brief statement about the company's mission and values, but do not include any information about the company's physical location.", "response": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 43, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "ground_truth": "Based on the information given in the passages, to force remove a printer in devices and printers, you need to go to Control Panel, then click on Hardware and Sound, and then on Printers. Right-click the printer that you want to remove, and click Delete. If it doesn't delete, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete. If your printer is connected to your computer via a USB, disconnect the cable, turn the printer on and off again, and ensure it is in a ready state. If you used Print Manager or Printers folder to remove a printer or printer port, close these applications and stop and restart the Spooler Service.", "response": "To force removal of a printer in devices and printers, follow these steps:\n1. Remove the printer from the devices list.\n2. Use Windows Devices and Printers to uninstall any Windows print drivers.\n3. If the printer is connected via USB, disconnect the cable and turn the printer off and on again to ensure it is in a ready state.\n4. In the Printers folder, right-click the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If unable to delete, right-click and select Run as administrator before clicking Delete.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 16}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 44, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are some strategies for guarding a tall person in basketball:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard them near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities (Passage 1).\n2. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, to guard a tall person in basketball, it is important to stay close to them and create a barrier between them and the basket. These strategies can help limit their shooting opportunities and make it more difficult for them to score.", "response": "Stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 10}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.06, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 45, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "health benefits to jalapenos", "ground_truth": "Jalapenos have numerous health benefits due to their capsaicin content. They have pain-killing properties and can serve as a natural nasal decongestant. They may also aid in weight loss and prevent heart disease, heart attacks, and possibly even cancer. Additionally, jalapenos are full of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants. They can also help increase cardiovascular health and defend heart health.", "response": "Jalapeno peppers have several health benefits, including pain relief, weight loss, natural nasal decongestant, potential prevention of heart disease, heart attack, and cancer, and being full of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 6}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 46, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "ground_truth": "To plant a potato that has sprouted, follow these steps:\n\n1. Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each using a sharp knife.\n2. Set the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and allow them to dry out for a cool, dark location overnight.\n3. Once the cut ends are dry, thoroughly wash the potatoes.\n4. Plant the potatoes in the ground, either whole or cut into cubes with a sprout on each cube.\n5. Space the potatoes about 6 to 8 inches apart and cover them with a layer of compost.\n6. Replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\n7. Water the potatoes regularly when the soil is dry to the touch.\n8. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines.", "response": "Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. Small potatoes can be planted whole. Water the potatoes thoroughly. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 47, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Rinse your hair completely with warm water, then use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair (Passage 1, step 6).\n2. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type, and apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand while in the shower (Passage 2, steps 1-3). Work the shampoo through your hair without piling it up on your head, and avoid tangling it while it's still wet.\n3. After applying shampoo, rinse your hair thoroughly with warm water, and then comb through it with your fingers to remove any remaining tangles (Passage 1, step 7).\n4. Apply a conditioner to your hair, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes before rinsing it out with cool water (Passage 1, step 8).\n5. To dry your hair, gently pat it with a towel or wrap it around your head to absorb excess water, avoiding rubbing it vigorously with a towel (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide instructions on how to style or dry your hair after cleaning it.", "response": "To properly clean your hair, follow these steps: Thoroughly wet the hair, apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, rinse the hair completely, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair, apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, and allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 14}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.08, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 48, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "ground_truth": "When you breathe in, your diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, expanding the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract to expand the ribcage. Pressure inside the chest is reduced, causing air to be sucked into the lungs. On the other hand, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. Air rich in carbon dioxide is then forced out of the lungs and windpipe. Breathing out does not require any effort from your body unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity.", "response": "When you breathe in, the diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest, and the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs. When you breathe out, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, and the intercostal muscles relax, reducing the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 49, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "benefits and side effects of drinking clove tea", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, the benefits of drinking clove tea include soothing the senses, relieving stress, providing relief from abdominal pain and aiding digestion. The side effects of drinking clove tea are not mentioned in the given passages.", "response": "Benefits of drinking clove tea include soothing the senses, relieving stress, and having skin benefits. It can also be used to relieve pain from muscle, joint, or ligament injuries, and soothe abdominal pain.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 1}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 50, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, it appears that watching Snapchat stories does not directly increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is increased by sending and receiving more snaps, and by interacting with friends on the platform. Watching stories is not mentioned as a factor that contributes to increasing one's score. Therefore, the answer to the question is: No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "response": "Unable to answer", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.6, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 51, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "response": "Children learn gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity with water play.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 4.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 15}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 52, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "ground_truth": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "response": "Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 2}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 77.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 53, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "ground_truth": "Based on the given passages, here is how the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs:\n\nWhen you inhale, the diaphragm muscle contracts, moving down from the bottom of your rib cage towards your abdominal region, which causes the thoracic cavity to increase in volume. This decrease in air pressure in the lungs below atmospheric pressure forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing you to inhale.\n\nTherefore, the air you breathe is processed by the diaphragm muscle before it reaches your lungs, which contracts to take air into the lungs and relax to let it out again. Additionally, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, such as oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment, which occurs in the lungs.", "response": "The diaphragm muscle contracts to take air into the lungs and relaxes to let it out.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 1.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 5}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 0, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "ground_truth": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "response": "Use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and top of the jamb. Pry up on the door stop until it comes loose and remove it. Set the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "best_surviving_path", "veto_total_penalty": 3.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 11}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": 1, "category": "", "sub_category": "unknown", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "ground_truth": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook pollock:\n\nPassage 1:\n\n* Spray a baking sheet with butter-flavored cooking spray.\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n* Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 2:\n\n* Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Bake the fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n* Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n* Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet.\n* Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\n\nTherefore, to cook pollock, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n2. Place the fillets on a baking sheet or in the oven.\n3. Cook the pollock until it flakes easily, either by baking it in the oven or on the stovetop.\n4. Add cheese to the pollock if desired and return it to the oven to melt the cheese.", "response": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees", "status": "success", "path_info": {"fallback_triggered": true, "fallback_source": "random_vetoed_path", "veto_total_penalty": 2.0, "veto_threshold_used": 0.45, "num_paths_explored": 24, "num_paths_vetoed": 9}, "layer_repair": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.7, "Status": "success"}}
